CC.provideCourse.bind(null,"office")({"lessons":{"office-01":{"html":"<p>University courses expect you to search academic sources, email instructors professionally, and recognize common online business models.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-smarter-web-searching\"><h2 id=\"smarter-web-searching\">Smarter web searching</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Operator</th><th>What it does</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>\"exact phrase\"</code></td><td>Matches words in that exact order</td><td><code>\"Istanbul Gelisim University\" syllabus</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>site:domain</code></td><td>Searches only inside one website/domain</td><td><code>site:edu.tr \"C programming\" notes</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>filetype:pdf</code></td><td>Finds downloadable documents (PDF, DOCX, PPTX)</td><td><code>\"database normalization\" filetype:pdf</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>-word</code></td><td>Excludes unwanted results</td><td><code>python tutorial -snake</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-professional-email-etiquette-to-cc-bcc\"><h2 id=\"professional-email-etiquette-to-cc-bcc\">Professional email etiquette (To, CC, BCC)</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>To</strong>: the main person(s) who need to read and reply.</li><li><strong>CC (Carbon Copy)</strong>: people who should stay informed (everyone sees their addresses).</li><li><strong>BCC (Blind Carbon Copy)</strong>: hidden recipients—use <strong>BCC</strong> when emailing a large group of students or clients so you do not leak everyone's email address!</li><li><strong>Subject line</strong>: short and specific (e.g., <code>CMP151 Sec 2 — Question about Lab 3</code>). Never leave it blank, and never write an entire paragraph in the subject.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-e-commerce-models\"><h2 id=\"e-commerce-models\">E-commerce models</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>B2C (Business-to-Consumer)</strong>: online store selling directly to individual shoppers (e.g., Trendyol retail, Amazon).</li><li><strong>B2B (Business-to-Business)</strong>: one company selling wholesale goods or software to another company (e.g., cloud hosting or bulk hardware).</li><li><strong>C2C (Consumer-to-Consumer)</strong>: individuals selling to other individuals via a platform (e.g., Sahibinden, Dolap).</li><li><strong>C2B (Consumer-to-Business)</strong>: individuals offering services/content to companies (e.g., freelance photographers selling stock photos or influencers).</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-how-the-web-works-in-one-minute\"><h2 id=\"how-the-web-works-in-one-minute\">How the web works in one minute</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Internet vs. Web.</strong> The <strong>Internet</strong> is the worldwide network of connected computers (the roads). The <strong>World Wide Web</strong> is one service that runs on it: pages linked together and opened in a browser (the shops on the roads). Email, online games and video calls also use the Internet but are not \"the Web\".</li><li><strong>URL</strong> (address): <code>https://www.gelisim.edu.tr/tr/page</code> = <strong>protocol</strong> (<code>https</code>) + <strong>domain name</strong> (<code>www.gelisim.edu.tr</code>) + <strong>path</strong> (<code>/tr/page</code>).</li><li><strong>HTTP vs. HTTPS.</strong> HTTP sends pages as plain text. <strong>HTTPS</strong> encrypts them (the <strong>padlock</strong> icon). Never type a password on a page without HTTPS.</li><li><strong>DNS</strong> turns a name like <code>gelisim.edu.tr</code> into the server's IP address — like a phone book.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-browser-settings-you-should-know\"><h2 id=\"browser-settings-you-should-know\">Browser settings you should know</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>What it is</th><th>Where (Chrome / Edge)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Cookies</strong></td><td>small files a website saves in your browser to remember you (login, cart, language)</td><td>Settings → Privacy and security → Cookies / Third-party cookies</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cache</strong></td><td>saved copies of page files so sites load faster</td><td>Settings → Privacy → <strong>Clear browsing data</strong> (<code>Ctrl+Shift+Delete</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>History</strong></td><td>list of pages you visited</td><td><code>Ctrl+H</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Private / Incognito window</strong></td><td>does <strong>not</strong> save history, cookies or form data after you close it (your school or ISP can still see traffic)</td><td><code>Ctrl+Shift+N</code> (Chrome) / <code>Ctrl+Shift+P</code> (Edge, Firefox)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Bookmarks / Favourites</strong></td><td>saved links</td><td><code>Ctrl+D</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Home page / startup</strong></td><td>page that opens first</td><td>Settings → On startup</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-email-threats\"><h2 id=\"email-threats\">Email threats</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Phishing:</strong> a fake email that pretends to be from your bank, university or a delivery company and asks you to \"verify your password\" on a fake site. Check the <strong>sender's real address</strong> and <strong>hover over links</strong> before clicking.</li><li><strong>Spam:</strong> unwanted mass email (adverts, scams). Mark it as spam; don't reply.</li><li><strong>Malicious attachments:</strong> files such as <code>.exe</code>, <code>.scr</code>, <code>.js</code> or Office files with <strong>macros</strong> that install malware when opened. Don't open attachments you were not expecting.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Email fields recap:</strong> <strong>To</strong> = main receivers · <strong>CC</strong> (carbon copy) = for information; everyone sees them · <strong>BCC</strong> (blind carbon copy) = hidden receivers; others cannot see these addresses (use it for mass emails to protect privacy).</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-all-five-e-commerce-models\"><h2 id=\"all-five-e-commerce-models\">All five e-commerce models</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Who sells → who buys</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>B2B</strong></td><td>business → business</td><td>a factory buys parts from a supplier</td></tr><tr><td><strong>B2C</strong></td><td>business → consumer</td><td>an online clothes shop</td></tr><tr><td><strong>C2C</strong></td><td>consumer → consumer</td><td>selling your old phone on a second-hand site</td></tr><tr><td><strong>B2G</strong></td><td>business → government</td><td>a company sells computers to a ministry through a public tender</td></tr><tr><td><strong>C2B</strong></td><td>consumer → business</td><td>a freelance photographer sells photos to a company</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Match the e-commerce models below, then complete the hands-on checklist:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"match\" data-set=\"ecommerce\"></div>\n<div class=\"widget checklist\" data-widget=\"checklist\" data-id=\"office/01-internet-services-ecommerce.md#1\"><div class=\"checklist-h\">Lesson 1 hands-on checklist</div><ul class=\"checks\"><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"0\"><span>Ran a Google search using <code>\"exact phrase\"</code> and <code>filetype:pdf</code></span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"1\"><span>Ran a search restricted to Turkish universities with <code>site:edu.tr</code></span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"2\"><span>Checked your university email inbox and practiced writing a clear Subject + greeting + sign-off</span></label></li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Putting 40 classmates in <strong>CC</strong> instead of <strong>BCC</strong>—that exposes everyone's private email address.</li><li>Writing <em>\"urgent\"</em> or <em>\"help\"</em> as an email subject without a course code or topic.</li><li>Confusing <strong>B2B</strong> (business selling to business) with <strong>C2C</strong> (person selling to person).</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>BCC (Blind Carbon Copy)</strong></td><td>email field that hides recipients' addresses from each other</td><td lang=\"tr\">gizli kopya (BCC)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>search operator</strong></td><td>special keyword (<code>site:</code>, <code>filetype:</code>, <code>\"\"</code>) that narrows web search results</td><td lang=\"tr\">arama operatörü</td></tr><tr><td><strong>B2C</strong></td><td>Business-to-Consumer e-commerce</td><td lang=\"tr\">işletmeden tüketiciye (B2C)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>B2B</strong></td><td>Business-to-Business e-commerce</td><td lang=\"tr\">işletmeden işletmeye (B2B)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"You want to email 35 classmates a group invitation without showing everyone's email address to the whole list. Which field should you put their addresses in?","opts":[{"h":"To","why":"everyone in <code>To</code> is visible to all recipients"},{"h":"CC","why":"everyone in <code>CC</code> is visible to all recipients"},{"h":"BCC","ok":1,"why":"Blind Carbon Copy hides recipients from each other"},{"h":"Subject","why":"Subject is the email title, not an address field"}],"why":"Always use BCC for bulk emails to protect recipients' privacy."},{"q":"Which search query finds only <strong>PDF</strong> files about SQL on <code>.edu.tr</code> university sites?","opts":[{"h":"<code>SQL pdf edu.tr</code>","why":"returns normal web pages mentioning those words"},{"h":"<code>SQL filetype:pdf site:edu.tr</code>","ok":1,"why":"restricts both file format (<code>pdf</code>) and domain (<code>edu.tr</code>)"},{"h":"<code>\"SQL\" -pdf</code>","why":"excludes the word <code>pdf</code>"},{"h":"<code>site:pdf filetype:edu.tr</code>","why":"<code>site:</code> and <code>filetype:</code> are swapped"}],"why":"Combine <code>filetype:pdf</code> and <code>site:edu.tr</code> to target university PDF handouts."},{"q":"A student sells a used textbook to another student on an online marketplace. Which e-commerce model is this?","opts":[{"h":"B2B","why":"business to business"},{"h":"B2C","why":"business to consumer"},{"h":"C2C","ok":1,"why":"Consumer-to-Consumer (two individuals trading via a platform)"},{"h":"C2B","why":"consumer selling to a business"}],"why":"Individuals selling to other individuals is C2C."}]],"id":"office-01","title":"Internet services, search operators, email, and e-commerce","goal":"use search operators effectively, write professional emails with To/CC/BCC, and classify e-commerce models","week":"1","minutes":15,"terms":[{"t":"BCC (Blind Carbon Copy)","m":"email field that hides recipients' addresses from each other","tr":"gizli kopya (BCC)"},{"t":"search operator","m":"special keyword (`site:`, `filetype:`, `\"\"`) that narrows web search results","tr":"arama operatörü"},{"t":"B2C","m":"Business-to-Consumer e-commerce","tr":"işletmeden tüketiciye (B2C)"},{"t":"B2B","m":"Business-to-Business e-commerce","tr":"işletmeden işletmeye (B2B)"}]},"office-02":{"html":"<p>In computer labs, knowing what a file extension means saves you from submitting the wrong file (like sending a <code>.lnk</code> shortcut instead of a <code>.docx</code> or <code>.pdf</code>!).</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-file-formats\"><h2 id=\"common-file-formats\">Common file formats</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Extension</th><th>What it is</th><th>Typical app</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>.docx</code></td><td>Editable Word document</td><td>Microsoft Word / LibreOffice Writer</td></tr><tr><td><code>.xlsx</code></td><td>Editable Excel spreadsheet</td><td>Microsoft Excel / LibreOffice Calc</td></tr><tr><td><code>.pptx</code></td><td>Editable PowerPoint presentation</td><td>Microsoft PowerPoint / Impress</td></tr><tr><td><code>.pdf</code></td><td>Fixed-layout document (looks identical on every device)</td><td>Adobe Reader / Web Browser</td></tr><tr><td><code>.txt</code></td><td>Plain unformatted text</td><td>Notepad / VS Code</td></tr><tr><td><code>.csv</code></td><td>Comma-Separated Values (plain-text table)</td><td>Excel / Python / SQL import</td></tr><tr><td><code>.zip</code></td><td>Compressed archive holding one or more files/folders</td><td>Windows Explorer / 7-Zip</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout-tip\"><div class=\"callout-h\">Show file extensions in Windows</div><p>In Windows File Explorer, click <strong>View → Show → File name extensions</strong> (Windows 11) or <strong>View → File name extensions</strong> (Windows 10) so you never confuse <code>report.pdf</code> with <code>report.pdf.exe</code>!</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-cloud-storage-sharing-permissions\"><h2 id=\"cloud-storage-sharing-permissions\">Cloud storage &amp; sharing permissions</h2>\n<p>Cloud drives (<strong>Google Drive</strong>, <strong>OneDrive</strong>) let you access files anywhere and collaborate in real time. When clicking <strong>Share</strong>, always check the permission level:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Viewer (Read-only)</strong>: can read and download, cannot edit. (Use this when sharing finished slides or notes!)</li><li><strong>Commenter</strong>: can add comments/suggestions without changing original text.</li><li><strong>Editor</strong>: can change or delete anything.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Match each file extension to its purpose, then complete the checklist:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"match\" data-set=\"formats\"></div>\n<div class=\"widget checklist\" data-widget=\"checklist\" data-id=\"office/02-file-formats-and-cloud.md#1\"><div class=\"checklist-h\">Lesson 2 hands-on checklist</div><ul class=\"checks\"><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"0\"><span>Turned on <strong>File name extensions</strong> in Windows File Explorer</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"1\"><span>Created a test folder with two files and compressed it into a <code>.zip</code> (<code>Right-click → Compress to ZIP file</code> / <code>Send to → Compressed (zipped) folder</code>)</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"2\"><span>Practiced setting a Google Drive / OneDrive share link to <strong>Viewer</strong> vs. <strong>Editor</strong></span></label></li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Submitting a <code>.pptx</code> or <code>.docx</code> when an assignment specifically asks for <strong><code>.pdf</code></strong> (fonts and layout shift if opened on another OS!).</li><li>Leaving a shared Google Drive link on <strong>\"Anyone with the link: Editor\"</strong> when you only meant for classmates to read it.</li><li>Trying to upload a whole folder to a form that only accepts one file—compress it into a <strong><code>.zip</code></strong> first!</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>file extension</strong></td><td>the suffix after the dot (<code>.docx</code>, <code>.pdf</code>, <code>.zip</code>) showing file format</td><td lang=\"tr\">dosya uzantısı</td></tr><tr><td><strong>PDF</strong></td><td>Portable Document Format — preserves exact page layout across devices</td><td lang=\"tr\">PDF formatı</td></tr><tr><td><strong>CSV</strong></td><td>Comma-Separated Values — plain-text table format</td><td lang=\"tr\">virgülle ayrılmış değerler</td></tr><tr><td><strong>ZIP archive</strong></td><td>a compressed single file bundling multiple files or folders</td><td lang=\"tr\">sıkıştırılmış arşiv</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"You finished your CV and want to email it so the layout, margins, and fonts look <strong>identical</strong> on the recruiter's computer. Which format should you export?","opts":[{"h":"<code>.txt</code>","why":"loses all formatting and fonts"},{"h":"<code>.docx</code>","why":"layout may shift if the recipient lacks your fonts"},{"h":"<code>.pdf</code>","ok":1,"why":"preserves exact layout and fonts across all systems"},{"h":"<code>.csv</code>","why":"CSV is for tabular data, not CVs"}],"why":"Export final documents to <code>.pdf</code> whenever layout consistency matters."},{"q":"Which file format stores tabular rows as plain text with commas between columns?","opts":[{"h":"<code>.pptx</code>","why":"PowerPoint slides"},{"h":"<code>.csv</code>","ok":1,"why":"Comma-Separated Values"},{"h":"<code>.zip</code>","why":"compressed archive"},{"h":"<code>.pdf</code>","why":"fixed-layout document"}],"why":"<code>.csv</code> is universal for importing/exporting spreadsheet and database tables."},{"q":"You want classmates to read your study notes on Google Drive <strong>without</strong> accidentally deleting paragraphs. Which permission should you grant?","opts":[{"h":"Editor","why":"Editor allows modifying and deleting content"},{"h":"Viewer","ok":1,"why":"Viewer allows reading without editing"},{"h":"Owner","why":"transfers ownership"},{"h":"Public Admin","why":"not a Drive sharing role"}],"why":"Grant <strong>Viewer</strong> access when people only need to read."}]],"id":"office-02","title":"File formats, compression, and cloud storage","goal":"identify common document, data, and archive file extensions and manage cloud sharing permissions safely","week":"1, 3","minutes":15,"terms":[{"t":"file extension","m":"the suffix after the dot (`.docx`, `.pdf`, `.zip`) showing file format","tr":"dosya uzantısı"},{"t":"PDF","m":"Portable Document Format — preserves exact page layout across devices","tr":"PDF formatı"},{"t":"CSV","m":"Comma-Separated Values — plain-text table format","tr":"virgülle ayrılmış değerler"},{"t":"ZIP archive","m":"a compressed single file bundling multiple files or folders","tr":"sıkıştırılmış arşiv"}]},"office-03":{"html":"<p><strong>Google Workspace</strong> (Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides, Forms, Sites) runs right in your browser with automatic saving and real-time multi-user editing.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-google-docs-collaboration\"><h2 id=\"google-docs-collaboration\">Google Docs collaboration</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Suggesting mode</strong> (top-right pencil icon → <strong>Suggesting</strong>): edits appear as colored tracked suggestions instead of overwriting text—great for group reports!</li><li><strong>Comments</strong> (<code>Insert → Comment</code> or <code>Ctrl+Alt+M</code>): tag a teammate with <code>@email</code> to assign a task.</li><li><strong>Version history</strong> (<code>File → Version history → See version history</code>): restore an earlier version if someone accidentally deletes a section.</li><li><strong>Download as Word/PDF</strong>: <code>File → Download → Microsoft Word (.docx)</code> or <code>PDF Document (.pdf)</code>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-google-forms-surveys-quizzes\"><h2 id=\"google-forms-surveys-quizzes\">Google Forms (surveys &amp; quizzes)</h2>\n<p>In <strong>Google Forms</strong> (<code>forms.google.com</code>):</p>\n<ol><li>Add questions: <strong>Multiple choice</strong>, <strong>Checkboxes</strong>, <strong>Short answer</strong>, <strong>Paragraph</strong>, or <strong>Linear scale</strong>.</li><li>Toggle <strong>Required</strong> on essential fields (like Student ID).</li><li>Click <strong>Settings → Make this a quiz</strong> to auto-grade MCQs.</li><li>Click <strong>Responses → Link to Sheets</strong> to collect every submission automatically in a spreadsheet!</li></ol>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-google-sites-quick-portfolio-or-project-page\"><h2 id=\"google-sites-quick-portfolio-or-project-page\">Google Sites (quick portfolio or project page)</h2>\n<p>In <strong>Google Sites</strong> (<code>sites.google.com</code>):</p>\n<ul><li>Add pages (<code>Pages</code> tab), drag content blocks (<code>Insert</code> tab), embed a Google Doc/Form/Slide directly, and click <strong>Publish</strong> to get a clean URL.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-every-google-forms-question-type\"><h2 id=\"every-google-forms-question-type\">Every Google Forms question type</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Use it for</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Short answer</strong></td><td>one line of text</td><td>Student ID</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Paragraph</strong></td><td>long text</td><td>\"Any comments?\"</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Multiple choice</strong></td><td>choose <strong>one</strong> option (round buttons)</td><td>Year of study</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Checkboxes</strong></td><td>choose <strong>one or more</strong> options (square boxes)</td><td>Which apps do you use?</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Dropdown</strong></td><td>choose one from a list that opens (saves space)</td><td>City</td></tr><tr><td><strong>File upload</strong></td><td>respondent uploads a file (needs a Google sign-in; files go to your Drive)</td><td>Upload your CV</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Linear scale</strong></td><td>a number on a scale, e.g. 1–5</td><td>\"How satisfied are you?\"</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Rating</strong></td><td>stars/hearts/thumbs</td><td>Rate the event</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Multiple choice grid</strong></td><td>one choice per row in a table</td><td>Rate each course: Poor / OK / Good</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Checkbox grid</strong></td><td>several choices per row</td><td>Which days can you attend each session?</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Date</strong> / <strong>Time</strong></td><td>a calendar date / a clock time</td><td>Date of birth / Preferred time</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Other useful settings: <strong>Required</strong> switch · <strong>Settings → Make this a quiz</strong> (answer keys and points) · <strong>Responses</strong> tab → <strong>Link to Sheets</strong> (all answers go into a Google Sheet) · <strong>Send</strong> button → link, email or embed code.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-google-calendar-and-meet\"><h2 id=\"google-calendar-and-meet\">Google Calendar and Meet</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Create an event:</strong> click a time slot or <strong>+ Create</strong> → add title, date and time.</li><li><strong>Invite people:</strong> type their emails under <strong>Add guests</strong>. They get an email and can answer <strong>Yes / No / Maybe</strong>. Guest permissions: <em>modify event, invite others, see guest list</em>.</li><li><strong>Video meeting:</strong> click <strong>Add Google Meet video conferencing</strong> — a Meet link is added to the event automatically.</li><li><strong>Recurring events:</strong> <em>Does not repeat</em> → <em>Weekly on Monday</em>… (e.g. a weekly class).</li><li><strong>Reminders:</strong> notification 10 minutes before, or an email.</li><li><strong>Share a calendar:</strong> Settings → <em>Share with specific people</em>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-google-drive-sharing-viewer-commenter-editor\"><h2 id=\"google-drive-sharing-viewer-commenter-editor\">Google Drive sharing (Viewer, Commenter, Editor)</h2>\n<p>Click <strong>Share</strong> on any file or folder:</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Can…</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Viewer</strong></td><td>only see the file</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Commenter</strong></td><td>see and add comments / suggestions, but not change the text</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Editor</strong></td><td>change everything, and (by default) share it with others</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>General access:</strong> <em>Restricted</em> (only added people) or <em>Anyone with the link</em>. <strong>File → Version history → See version history</strong> (<code>Ctrl+Alt+Shift+H</code>) shows every earlier version and lets you <strong>restore</strong> one. Several people can type in the same Docs/Sheets/Slides file <strong>at the same time</strong> (real-time collaboration) — each person has a coloured cursor.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<div class=\"widget checklist\" data-widget=\"checklist\" data-id=\"office/03-google-workspace-docs-forms.md#1\"><div class=\"checklist-h\">Lesson 3 hands-on checklist</div><ul class=\"checks\"><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"0\"><span>Opened Google Docs, switched to <strong>Suggesting</strong> mode, and added one comment</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"1\"><span>Checked <code>File → Version history → See version history</code></span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"2\"><span>Created a 3-question Google Form and linked it to a <strong>Google Sheet</strong> under the <strong>Responses</strong> tab</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"3\"><span>Explored <code>File → Download → PDF Document (.pdf)</code> in Google Docs</span></label></li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Forgetting to toggle <strong>Required</strong> on key fields like Name or Student ID in Google Forms.</li><li>Turning on <strong>\"Restrict to organization users\"</strong> in Form Settings when external users also need to fill it out.</li><li>Editing directly in <strong>Editing</strong> mode when reviewing a teammate's draft instead of <strong>Suggesting</strong> mode.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Suggesting mode</strong></td><td>Google Docs mode that proposes edits for review without permanent overwrite</td><td lang=\"tr\">öneri modu</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Version history</strong></td><td>timeline of saved snapshots allowing rollback to earlier drafts</td><td lang=\"tr\">sürüm geçmişi</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Google Forms</strong></td><td>web tool for surveys and quizzes that exports responses to Google Sheets</td><td lang=\"tr\">Google Formlar</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"In Google Docs, which mode lets you propose changes to a teammate's paragraph so they can accept or reject each edit?","opts":[{"h":"Viewing","why":"read-only"},{"h":"Suggesting","ok":1,"why":"marks insertions/deletions for approval"},{"h":"Printing","why":"print layout preview"},{"h":"Offline","why":"allows editing without internet"}],"why":"Suggesting mode works like Track Changes in Microsoft Word."},{"q":"Where do you go in Google Docs to recover a paragraph deleted two hours ago?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Edit → Undo</code> only","why":"Undo only steps back within the current session"},{"h":"<code>File → Version history → See version history</code>","ok":1,"why":"stores timestamped snapshots across sessions"},{"h":"<code>Tools → Word count</code>","why":"counts words/characters"},{"h":"<code>View → Print layout</code>","why":"toggles page view"}],"why":"Version history lets you inspect and restore previous saved states."},{"q":"How do you automatically save every Google Form submission into a table for analysis?","opts":[{"h":"Screenshot each response","why":"manual and error-prone"},{"h":"Under the <strong>Responses</strong> tab, click <strong>Link to Sheets</strong>","ok":1,"why":"streams every new submission into a Google Sheet"},{"h":"Export to <code>.pptx</code>","why":"PowerPoint is for slides"},{"h":"Copy from <code>Tools → Script</code>","why":"unnecessary"}],"why":"Linking a Form to Google Sheets creates a live spreadsheet of responses."}]],"id":"office-03","title":"Google Workspace — Docs, Forms, and Sites","goal":"collaborate in Google Docs, build a Google Form survey, and structure a simple Google Site","week":"2–3","minutes":15,"terms":[{"t":"Suggesting mode","m":"Google Docs mode that proposes edits for review without permanent overwrite","tr":"öneri modu"},{"t":"Version history","m":"timeline of saved snapshots allowing rollback to earlier drafts","tr":"sürüm geçmişi"},{"t":"Google Forms","m":"web tool for surveys and quizzes that exports responses to Google Sheets","tr":"Google Formlar"}]},"office-04":{"html":"<p><strong>Microsoft Word</strong> is the standard tool for lab reports, assignments, and CVs. Clean formatting and keyboard shortcuts save hours every semester.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-core-ribbon-paths-microsoft-365-word\"><h2 id=\"core-ribbon-paths-microsoft-365-word\">Core Ribbon paths (Microsoft 365 / Word)</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Font &amp; size</strong>: <code>Home → Font</code> group (e.g., Calibri/Arial/Times New Roman 11–12 pt).</li><li><strong>Paragraph alignment &amp; spacing</strong>: <code>Home → Paragraph</code> group (Left, Center, Right, <strong>Justify</strong> <code>Ctrl+J</code>; Line and Paragraph Spacing → <code>1.15</code> or <code>1.5</code>).</li><li><strong>Format Painter</strong>: <code>Home → Clipboard → Format Painter</code> (copies formatting from one selection to another; double-click to paint multiple places!).</li><li><strong>Find &amp; Replace</strong>: <code>Home → Editing → Replace</code> (<code>Ctrl+H</code>)—great for fixing a misspelled term across a 20-page report in one click.</li><li><strong>Show/Hide formatting marks</strong>: <code>Home → Paragraph → ¶</code> (<code>Ctrl+*</code>)—reveals hidden spaces, tabs, and Enter breaks.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-essential-shortcuts\"><h2 id=\"essential-shortcuts\">Essential shortcuts</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Shortcut</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Ctrl+C</code> / <code>Ctrl+X</code> / <code>Ctrl+V</code></td><td>Copy / Cut / Paste</td></tr><tr><td><code>Ctrl+Z</code> / <code>Ctrl+Y</code></td><td>Undo / Redo</td></tr><tr><td><code>Ctrl+B</code> / <code>Ctrl+I</code> / <code>Ctrl+U</code></td><td>Bold / Italic / Underline</td></tr><tr><td><code>Ctrl+F</code> / <code>Ctrl+H</code></td><td>Find / Find &amp; Replace</td></tr><tr><td><code>Ctrl+S</code> / <code>Ctrl+P</code></td><td>Save / Print</td></tr><tr><td><code>Ctrl+A</code></td><td>Select All</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-the-word-window-and-file-security\"><h2 id=\"the-word-window-and-file-security\">The Word window and file security</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Ribbon:</strong> the tabs at the top (File, Home, Insert, Design/Draw, Layout, References, Mailings, Review, View). Each tab has <strong>groups</strong> of buttons. <code>Ctrl+F1</code> hides/shows the ribbon.</li><li><strong>Quick Access Toolbar (QAT):</strong> the small toolbar with Save / Undo / Redo. Add any button: right-click it → <strong>Add to Quick Access Toolbar</strong>.</li><li><strong>Backstage view:</strong> everything you see after clicking <strong>File</strong> — New, Open, Save As, Print, Info, Export, Options.</li><li><strong>File formats:</strong> <code>.docx</code> (normal Word document) · <code>.doc</code> (old Word 97–2003) · <code>.dotx</code> (<strong>template</strong>) · <code>.docm</code> (document with macros) · <code>.pdf</code> (fixed layout, for sharing/printing) · <code>.rtf</code> / <code>.txt</code>.</li><li><strong>AutoSave:</strong> the switch at the top-left. It saves every few seconds, but only for files stored in <strong>OneDrive / SharePoint</strong>. AutoRecover (File → Options → Save) saves a backup copy every <em>n</em> minutes for local files.</li><li><strong>Protect Document:</strong> <strong>File → Info → Protect Document</strong> → <em>Always Open Read-Only</em>, <strong>Encrypt with Password</strong> (needs a password to open), <strong>Restrict Editing</strong> (only comments / only form filling), <em>Add a Digital Signature</em>, <strong>Mark as Final</strong>.</li><li><strong>Inspect Document:</strong> <strong>File → Info → Check for Issues → Inspect Document</strong> finds and removes hidden data (comments, tracked changes, author name, hidden text) before you share a file. <em>Check Accessibility</em> and <em>Check Compatibility</em> are in the same menu.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-formatting-tools-named-in-the-exam\"><h2 id=\"formatting-tools-named-in-the-exam\">Formatting tools named in the exam</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Format Painter</strong> (Home → Clipboard, the paintbrush): copies formatting. <strong>Click</strong> once to use once; <strong>double-click</strong> to paint many places; <code>Esc</code> to stop. Shortcut: <code>Ctrl+Shift+C</code> / <code>Ctrl+Shift+V</code>.</li><li><strong>Borders and Shading:</strong> Home → Paragraph → Borders arrow → <strong>Borders and Shading…</strong> (paragraph borders, <strong>Page Border</strong> tab, shading colour). Page borders are also under <strong>Design → Page Borders</strong>.</li><li><strong>Columns:</strong> Layout → <strong>Columns</strong> → Two / Three / More Columns… (newsletter style). Insert a column break: Layout → Breaks → <strong>Column</strong> (<code>Ctrl+Shift+Enter</code>).</li><li><strong>Bullets and Numbering:</strong> Home → Paragraph. <code>Tab</code> makes a lower level; <code>Shift+Tab</code> a higher level.</li><li><strong>Tabs:</strong> click the ruler to set a tab stop; the tab selector (left of the ruler) chooses Left / Center / Right / Decimal tab.</li><li><strong>Margins, Orientation, Size:</strong> Layout → Page Setup.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Practice matching shortcuts below, then complete the Word formatting checklist:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"match\" data-set=\"shortcuts\"></div>\n<div class=\"widget checklist\" data-widget=\"checklist\" data-id=\"office/04-word-basics-formatting.md#1\"><div class=\"checklist-h\">Lesson 4 hands-on checklist</div><ul class=\"checks\"><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"0\"><span>Opened Word (or Google Docs) and formatted a paragraph with <strong>Justify</strong> (<code>Ctrl+J</code>) and <strong>1.5 line spacing</strong></span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"1\"><span>Used <strong>Format Painter</strong> (<code>Home → Clipboard → Format Painter</code>) to copy heading formatting</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"2\"><span>Pressed <code>Ctrl+H</code> to replace one word across the document</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"3\"><span>Toggled <code>¶</code> (<code>Home → Paragraph → ¶</code>) to inspect spaces and line breaks</span></label></li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Pressing <code>Space</code> ten times to center a title instead of using <strong>Center align</strong> (<code>Ctrl+E</code>).</li><li>Pressing <code>Enter</code> ten times to start a new page—later edits push everything down! Use <strong>Page Break</strong> (<code>Ctrl+Enter</code>) instead.</li><li>Pressing <code>Ctrl+V</code> when pasting from a website and bringing ugly background colors—use <strong>Paste Special → Keep Text Only</strong> (<code>Ctrl+Shift+V</code>).</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Format Painter</strong></td><td>Word tool that copies font and paragraph styling from one text block to another</td><td lang=\"tr\">biçim boyacısı</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Justify</strong></td><td>alignment that stretches lines evenly to both left and right margins</td><td lang=\"tr\">iki yana yasla</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Find &amp; Replace</strong></td><td>tool (<code>Ctrl+H</code>) that searches for text and swaps it with new text</td><td lang=\"tr\">bul ve değiştir</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"Which keyboard shortcut opens <strong>Find &amp; Replace</strong> in Microsoft Word?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Ctrl+F</code>","why":"opens Find only"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+H</code>","ok":1,"why":"opens Find and Replace"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+R</code>","why":"right-aligns paragraph in Word"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+B</code>","why":"toggles Bold"}],"why":"<code>Ctrl+H</code> opens the Replace tab directly."},{"q":"What happens if you <strong>double-click</strong> the <strong>Format Painter</strong> button (<code>Home → Clipboard</code>)?","opts":[{"h":"It deletes all formatting","why":"that is Clear All Formatting"},{"h":"It stays active so you can apply the copied formatting to multiple selections until you press <code>Esc</code>","ok":1,"why":"single-click applies once; double-click locks it on"},{"h":"It saves the document","why":"<code>Ctrl+S</code> saves"},{"h":"It opens Font settings","why":"<code>Ctrl+D</code> opens Font dialog"}],"why":"Double-clicking Format Painter lets you format several items in a row."},{"q":"Why should you avoid pressing <code>Space</code> repeatedly to align text in Word?","opts":[{"h":"Word bans multiple spaces","why":"Word allows them, they just break easily"},{"h":"Different fonts, margins, or PDF exports will shift the alignment","ok":1,"why":"use Alignment buttons or Tab stops instead"},{"h":"It deletes the paragraph","why":"it does not delete text"},{"h":"It doubles the file size","why":"negligible size impact"}],"why":"Always use paragraph alignment or tabs, never repeated spaces."}]],"id":"office-04","title":"Microsoft Word — Basics, formatting, and shortcuts","goal":"format text and paragraphs cleanly in Microsoft Word, use Find & Replace, and apply core keyboard shortcuts","week":"4–5","minutes":16,"terms":[{"t":"Format Painter","m":"Word tool that copies font and paragraph styling from one text block to another","tr":"biçim boyacısı"},{"t":"Justify","m":"alignment that stretches lines evenly to both left and right margins","tr":"iki yana yasla"},{"t":"Find & Replace","m":"tool (`Ctrl+H`) that searches for text and swaps it with new text","tr":"bul ve değiştir"}]},"office-05":{"html":"<p>Long university reports look messy if you build the Table of Contents by hand. Using <strong>Styles</strong> lets Word build and update it in one click.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-styles-automatic-table-of-contents-toc\"><h2 id=\"styles-automatic-table-of-contents-toc\">Styles &amp; Automatic Table of Contents (TOC)</h2>\n<ol><li><strong>Apply Heading styles</strong>: Instead of just making a title bold and big, select it and click <code>Home → Styles → Heading 1</code> (for main chapters) and <code>Heading 2</code> (for sub-sections).</li><li><strong>Insert TOC</strong>: Place your cursor at the start of the document and click: <code>References → Table of Contents → Automatic Table 1</code></li><li><strong>Update after edits</strong>: Right-click the TOC → <strong>Update Field → Update entire table</strong> (or <code>Update page numbers only</code>).</li></ol>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-page-breaks-vs-section-breaks\"><h2 id=\"page-breaks-vs-section-breaks\">Page breaks vs. Section breaks</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Page Break</strong> (<code>Insert → Pages → Page Break</code>, or <code>Ctrl+Enter</code>): starts the next text cleanly at the top of a new page.</li><li><strong>Section Break (Next Page)</strong> (<code>Layout → Page Setup → Breaks → Next Page</code>): splits the document into independent <strong>sections</strong> so you can have <strong>portrait</strong> pages in Chapter 1 and <strong>landscape</strong> in Chapter 2, or omit page numbers on the cover page!</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-headers-footers-page-numbers\"><h2 id=\"headers-footers-page-numbers\">Headers, footers &amp; page numbers</h2>\n<ul><li><code>Insert → Header &amp; Footer → Page Number → Bottom of Page</code></li><li>To hide the page number on Page 1 (your cover page): double-click the header/footer to open <strong>Header &amp; Footer</strong> tab → tick <strong>Different First Page</strong>.</li><li>Margins &amp; Orientation: <code>Layout → Page Setup → Margins / Orientation / Size</code>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<div class=\"widget checklist\" data-widget=\"checklist\" data-id=\"office/05-word-styles-toc-headers.md#1\"><div class=\"checklist-h\">Lesson 5 hands-on checklist</div><ul class=\"checks\"><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"0\"><span>Styled 3 titles with <code>Home → Styles → Heading 1</code> and 2 subheadings with <code>Heading 2</code></span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"1\"><span>Inserted an automatic Table of Contents via <code>References → Table of Contents</code></span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"2\"><span>Inserted a clean <strong>Page Break</strong> (<code>Ctrl+Enter</code>) before a new section</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"3\"><span>Added page numbers (<code>Insert → Page Number</code>) and enabled <strong>Different First Page</strong></span></label></li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Typing a Table of Contents manually—every time you add a paragraph, all page numbers become wrong!</li><li>Seeing <em>\"No table of contents entries found\"</em> because you made headings <strong>Bold + 16pt</strong> manually instead of applying <strong>Heading 1 / Heading 2</strong> styles.</li><li>Changing <strong>Orientation</strong> to Landscape without a <strong>Section Break</strong>, which flips the entire document sideways instead of just one wide table page.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Style</strong></td><td>a named bundle of font and paragraph settings (<code>Heading 1</code>, <code>Normal</code>)</td><td lang=\"tr\">stil</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Table of Contents</strong></td><td>an auto-generated list of headings and page numbers (<code>References → Table of Contents</code>)</td><td lang=\"tr\">içindekiler tablosu</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Section Break</strong></td><td>a break dividing a document so different sections can have separate layouts or headers</td><td lang=\"tr\">bölüm sonu</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"Word says <em>\"No table of contents entries found\"</em> when you click <code>References → Table of Contents</code>. Why?","opts":[{"h":"Your document has too few pages","why":"TOC works on 1-page documents too"},{"h":"You formatted titles manually (bold/large) instead of applying <code>Home → Styles → Heading 1/2</code>","ok":1,"why":"Automatic TOC only reads Heading styles"},{"h":"You forgot to save as <code>.pdf</code>","why":"TOC is built inside <code>.docx</code>"},{"h":"Your margins are too narrow","why":"margins do not affect TOC detection"}],"why":"Automatic Table of Contents pulls entries from <code>Heading 1</code>, <code>Heading 2</code>, etc."},{"q":"Which shortcut inserts a clean <strong>Page Break</strong> so a new chapter always begins at the top of the next page?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Shift+Enter</code>","why":"inserts a soft line break within the same paragraph"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+Enter</code>","ok":1,"why":"inserts a hard Page Break"},{"h":"<code>Alt+Enter</code>","why":"repeats last action / new line in Excel cell"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+Shift+Enter</code>","why":"column break"}],"why":"<code>Ctrl+Enter</code> inserts a Page Break."},{"q":"You want <strong>Page 3</strong> of a portrait report to be <strong>Landscape</strong> for a wide table, while keeping Pages 1, 2, and 4 <strong>Portrait</strong>. What must you insert before and after Page 3?","opts":[{"h":"Page Breaks (<code>Ctrl+Enter</code>)","why":"Page Breaks share the same page orientation"},{"h":"Section Breaks (<code>Layout → Breaks → Next Page</code>)","ok":1,"why":"Section Breaks allow independent orientation per section"},{"h":"Tab stops","why":"tab stops align text on a line"},{"h":"Footnotes","why":"footnotes sit at the bottom of a page"}],"why":"Only Section Breaks allow mixed Portrait and Landscape pages in one document."}]],"id":"office-05","title":"Microsoft Word — Styles, Table of Contents, and Page Layout","goal":"apply Heading styles, generate an automatic Table of Contents, and configure page breaks, headers, footers, and page numbers","week":"5","minutes":18,"terms":[{"t":"Style","m":"a named bundle of font and paragraph settings (`Heading 1`, `Normal`)","tr":"stil"},{"t":"Table of Contents","m":"an auto-generated list of headings and page numbers (`References → Table of Contents`)","tr":"içindekiler tablosu"},{"t":"Section Break","m":"a break dividing a document so different sections can have separate layouts or headers","tr":"bölüm sonu"}]},"office-06":{"html":"<p>Academic and technical reports require structured <strong>tables</strong>, numbered <strong>figures</strong>, <strong>citations</strong>, and <strong>reviewing tools</strong>.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-tables-captions\"><h2 id=\"tables-captions\">Tables &amp; captions</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Insert Table</strong>: <code>Insert → Tables → Table</code> (choose rows × columns). Use <strong>Table Design</strong> and <strong>Layout</strong> tabs (which appear when your cursor is inside the table) to merge cells, shade headers, and repeat header rows across pages (<strong>Repeat Header Rows</strong>).</li><li><strong>Captions for figures/tables</strong>: Right-click an image or table → <strong>Insert Caption</strong> (e.g., <code>Figure 1: Network topology</code>) or <code>References → Captions → Insert Caption</code>. Word automatically renumbers captions if you insert a new figure earlier!</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-citations-bibliography\"><h2 id=\"citations-bibliography\">Citations &amp; Bibliography</h2>\n<p>Under <code>References → Citations &amp; Bibliography</code>:</p>\n<ol><li>Choose <strong>Style</strong> (e.g., <code>APA</code> or <code>IEEE</code>).</li><li>Click <strong>Insert Citation → Add New Source</strong> to enter author, title, and year.</li><li>At the end of your report, click <strong>Bibliography → Insert Bibliography</strong> to generate a formatted reference list.</li></ol>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-reviewing-exporting\"><h2 id=\"reviewing-exporting\">Reviewing &amp; exporting</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Track Changes</strong>: <code>Review → Tracking → Track Changes</code> (<code>Ctrl+Shift+E</code>) highlights every insertion and deletion for group editing.</li><li><strong>Export to PDF</strong>: <code>File → Save As</code> (choose <code>PDF (*.pdf)</code>) or <code>File → Export → Create PDF/XPS</code>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-editing-helpers-autocorrect-paste-special-find-replace-go-to\"><h2 id=\"editing-helpers-autocorrect-paste-special-find-replace-go-to\">Editing helpers: AutoCorrect, Paste Special, Find/Replace/Go To</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>AutoCorrect</strong> fixes typing mistakes automatically (<em>teh → the</em>, <code>(c)</code> → ©). <strong>File → Options → Proofing → AutoCorrect Options…</strong> — add your own entries or turn rules off. Press <code>Ctrl+Z</code> straight after an unwanted correction to undo it.</li><li><strong>Paste Special:</strong> Home → Paste arrow → <strong>Paste Special…</strong> (<code>Ctrl+Alt+V</code>). Choose <strong>Unformatted Text</strong> to remove the source formatting, or paste as a picture / link. The small <strong>Paste Options</strong> button offers <em>Keep Source Formatting</em>, <em>Merge Formatting</em>, <em>Keep Text Only</em>.</li><li><strong>Find</strong> <code>Ctrl+F</code> (Navigation pane) · <strong>Replace</strong> <code>Ctrl+H</code> (Replace All changes every match) · <strong>Go To</strong> <code>Ctrl+G</code> or <code>F5</code> (jump to a page, section, line, bookmark, table…).</li><li><strong>Templates:</strong> File → <strong>New</strong> → search online templates (CV, letter, report) or save your own as <strong>Word Template (*.dotx)</strong>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<div class=\"widget checklist\" data-widget=\"checklist\" data-id=\"office/06-word-tables-citations-pdf.md#1\"><div class=\"checklist-h\">Lesson 6 hands-on checklist</div><ul class=\"checks\"><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"0\"><span>Inserted a 3×4 table (<code>Insert → Table</code>) with a shaded header row</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"1\"><span>Added a numbered caption (<code>References → Insert Caption</code>) below an image or table</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"2\"><span>Added one sample source via <code>References → Insert Citation</code> and generated a Bibliography</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"3\"><span>Toggled <strong>Track Changes</strong> (<code>Review → Track Changes</code>), made an edit, and accepted it</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"4\"><span>Exported the document to <strong><code>.pdf</code></strong> (<code>File → Export → Create PDF/XPS</code>)</span></label></li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Numbering figures manually (<code>Figure 1</code>, <code>Figure 2</code>…) and forgetting to renumber <code>Figure 2</code>–<code>Figure 10</code> after inserting a new image at the top. Use <strong>Insert Caption</strong>!</li><li>Sending a <code>.docx</code> with <strong>Track Changes</strong> still unaccepted/visible when submitting a final assignment—always <strong>Accept All Changes</strong> and turn Track Changes off before final PDF export.</li><li>Copying bibliography text with mixed fonts instead of using <code>References → Bibliography</code>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>caption</strong></td><td>an auto-numbered label (<code>Figure 1</code>, <code>Table 1</code>) attached to an image or table</td><td lang=\"tr\">resim yazısı / başlık</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Track Changes</strong></td><td>Word reviewing mode that records every edit for acceptance or rejection</td><td lang=\"tr\">değişiklikleri izle</td></tr><tr><td><strong>bibliography</strong></td><td>the formatted list of cited sources at the end of a document</td><td lang=\"tr\">kaynakça</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"Where in Microsoft Word do you turn on <strong>Track Changes</strong> to review edits made by teammates?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Home → Styles</code>","why":"Styles format headings"},{"h":"<code>Insert → Comments</code>","why":"inserts comments only"},{"h":"<code>Review → Tracking → Track Changes</code>","ok":1,"why":"records insertions, deletions, and formatting changes"},{"h":"<code>References → Captions</code>","why":"numbers figures and tables"}],"why":"Track Changes lives under the <strong>Review</strong> tab."},{"q":"Why is <code>References → Insert Caption</code> better than typing <code>\"Figure 1\"</code> as normal text below an image?","opts":[{"h":"It makes the image higher resolution","why":"captions don't alter image pixels"},{"h":"Word automatically renumbers all figures if you add or move one, and can build a List of Figures","ok":1,"why":"saves manual renumbering errors"},{"h":"It converts the image to PDF","why":"unrelated"},{"h":"It prevents copying","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"Auto-captions keep numbering consistent and allow a List of Figures."},{"q":"Before submitting a final report exported from Word, what should you check if <strong>Track Changes</strong> was used?","opts":[{"h":"Delete the whole file","why":"no need"},{"h":"Accept (or Reject) all changes and turn Track Changes off before exporting to PDF","ok":1,"why":"ensures red/strikethrough markups don't appear in the final PDF"},{"h":"Hide page numbers","why":"unrelated"},{"h":"Change margins to 0","why":"breaks printing"}],"why":"Always resolve tracked changes before final submission."}]],"id":"office-06","title":"Microsoft Word — Tables, captions, citations, and PDF export","goal":"insert formatted tables and figure captions, manage citations and Track Changes, and export to PDF","week":"6","minutes":16,"terms":[{"t":"caption","m":"an auto-numbered label (`Figure 1`, `Table 1`) attached to an image or table","tr":"resim yazısı / başlık"},{"t":"Track Changes","m":"Word reviewing mode that records every edit for acceptance or rejection","tr":"değişiklikleri izle"},{"t":"bibliography","m":"the formatted list of cited sources at the end of a document","tr":"kaynakça"}]},"office-07":{"html":"<p><strong>Microsoft Excel</strong> (and <strong>Google Sheets</strong>) organizes data into grids of <strong>columns</strong> (<code>A, B, C...</code>) and <strong>rows</strong> (<code>1, 2, 3...</code>). Each box is a <strong>cell</strong> named by its column + row (e.g., <code>B3</code>).</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-workbooks-sheets-and-ranges\"><h2 id=\"workbooks-sheets-and-ranges\">Workbooks, sheets, and ranges</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Workbook</strong>: the entire <code>.xlsx</code> file.</li><li><strong>Worksheet</strong>: one tab at the bottom (<code>Sheet1</code>, <code>Grades</code>).</li><li><strong>Range</strong>: a rectangular block of cells written with a colon, e.g., <code>A1:C10</code>.</li><li><strong>Number formatting</strong> (<code>Home → Number</code>): format cells as <strong>Currency</strong> (<code>₺</code>), <strong>Percentage</strong> (<code>%</code>), <strong>Date</strong>, or <strong>2 Decimal Places</strong> (<code>0.00</code>). Never type <code>\"TL\"</code> or <code>\"%\"</code> as plain text inside a number if you want to calculate with it!</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-relative-vs-absolute-references-the-1-excel-exam-topic\"><h2 id=\"relative-vs-absolute-references-the-1-excel-exam-topic\">Relative vs. Absolute references (the #1 Excel exam topic!)</h2>\n<p>When you drag a formula down or across using the <strong>fill handle</strong> (bottom-right corner of a cell):</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Reference</th><th>Syntax</th><th>Behavior when copied</th><th>Example use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Relative</strong></td><td><code>B2</code></td><td>Row &amp; column <strong>shift</strong> automatically</td><td><code>=B2*C2</code> dragged down becomes <code>=B3*C3</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Absolute</strong></td><td><code>$B$2</code></td><td>Both column &amp; row stay <strong>locked</strong></td><td><code>=B2*$F$1</code> (multiplying every row by one tax rate in <code>F1</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Mixed</strong></td><td><code>$B2</code> or <code>B$2</code></td><td>Only the <code>$</code> part stays locked</td><td>Multiplication tables</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><em>(Shortcut: press <strong><code>F4</code></strong> while your cursor is on <code>F1</code> in the formula bar to cycle through <code>F1</code> → <code>$F$1</code> → <code>F$1</code> → <code>$F1</code>!)</em></p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-moving-around-a-worksheet-quickly\"><h2 id=\"moving-around-a-worksheet-quickly\">Moving around a worksheet quickly</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Keys</th><th>Moves to</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Ctrl+Home</code></td><td>cell <strong>A1</strong></td></tr><tr><td><code>Ctrl+End</code></td><td>the last used cell</td></tr><tr><td><code>Ctrl+→ / ↓ / ← / ↑</code></td><td>the edge of the current data block</td></tr><tr><td><code>Ctrl+PgDn / PgUp</code></td><td>next / previous <strong>sheet</strong></td></tr><tr><td><code>F5</code> or <code>Ctrl+G</code></td><td><strong>Go To</strong> a cell address</td></tr><tr><td><code>Ctrl+Space</code> / <code>Shift+Space</code></td><td>select the whole column / row</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Freeze Panes</strong> (View → Freeze Panes → <em>Freeze Top Row</em> / <em>Freeze First Column</em> / <em>Freeze Panes</em> at the selected cell) keeps headings visible while you scroll. <strong>Cursor shapes:</strong> white thick cross = select · thin black <strong>+</strong> at the cell corner = <strong>fill handle</strong> (copy/series) · four-headed arrow = move cells. <strong>Save formats:</strong> <code>.xlsx</code> (normal), <code>.xlsm</code> (with macros), <code>.xls</code> (old), <strong><code>.csv</code></strong> (plain text, commas, only the active sheet and no formatting or formulas — just values), <code>.pdf</code>.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<div class=\"widget checklist\" data-widget=\"checklist\" data-id=\"office/07-excel-basics-references.md#1\"><div class=\"checklist-h\">Lesson 7 hands-on checklist</div><ul class=\"checks\"><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"0\"><span>Created a small 4-row price table (<code>Item</code>, <code>Qty</code>, <code>Unit Price</code>, <code>Total</code>)</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"1\"><span>Formatted prices as Currency/Number (<code>Home → Number</code>) without typing <code>\"TL\"</code> into the number</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"2\"><span>Put a tax rate <code>0.20</code> in <code>F1</code> and wrote <code>=D2*$F$1</code>, then dragged it down to verify <code>$F$1</code> stayed locked</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"3\"><span>Tested <code>F4</code> in the formula bar to toggle <code>$</code> locks</span></label></li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Forgetting <code>$</code> around a fixed tax/bonus cell (<code>F1</code>) before dragging a formula down—Row 3 then multiplies by empty <code>F2</code> (<code>0</code>)!</li><li>Typing <code>\"20 TL\"</code> as text instead of <code>20</code> formatted as Currency—text cannot be summed (<code>SUM</code> ignores text!).</li><li>Seeing <code>###</code> in a cell and thinking it's an error—<code>###</code> just means the <strong>column is too narrow</strong>; double-click the column border to auto-fit!</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>cell reference</strong></td><td>a cell's coordinate such as <code>B3</code> or <code>$F$1</code></td><td lang=\"tr\">hücre başvurusu</td></tr><tr><td><strong>relative reference</strong></td><td>a reference (<code>A1</code>) that shifts automatically when copied</td><td lang=\"tr\">göreli başvuru</td></tr><tr><td><strong>absolute reference</strong></td><td>a locked reference (<code>$A$1</code>) that never changes when copied</td><td lang=\"tr\">mutlak başvuru</td></tr><tr><td><strong>fill handle</strong></td><td>the small square at the bottom-right of a selected cell used to copy formulas</td><td lang=\"tr\">doldurma tutamacı</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"Cell <code>C2</code> contains <code>=B2*E1</code>. You drag the fill handle down one row into <code>C3</code>. What does <code>C3</code> become?","opts":[{"h":"<code>=B2*E1</code>","why":"neither has <code>$</code>, so both shift"},{"h":"<code>=B3*E2</code>","ok":1,"why":"both relative references move down 1 row"},{"h":"<code>=B3*E1</code>","why":"<code>E1</code> has no <code>$</code>, so it also shifts to <code>E2</code>"},{"h":"<code>=C3*F2</code>","why":"dragging down changes rows, not columns"}],"why":"Without <code>$</code> locks, dragging down 1 row increments every row number by 1."},{"q":"You want every row in <code>D2:D10</code> to multiply by a single discount rate stored in <code>H1</code>. Which formula should you write in <code>D2</code> before dragging down?","opts":[{"h":"<code>=C2*H1</code>","why":"<code>H1</code> will shift to <code>H2, H3...</code>"},{"h":"<code>=C2*$H$1</code>","ok":1,"why":"<code>$H$1</code> stays locked on <code>H1</code> in every row"},{"h":"<code>=$C$2*H1</code>","why":"locks <code>C2</code> instead of <code>H1</code>"},{"h":"<code>=C2*H$2</code>","why":"points to <code>H2</code>, not <code>H1</code>"}],"why":"Lock the single rate cell with <code>$H$1</code>."},{"q":"What does <code>###</code> displayed inside an Excel cell mean?","opts":[{"h":"Division by zero","why":"that shows <code>#DIV/0!</code>"},{"h":"Invalid formula name","why":"that shows <code>#NAME?</code>"},{"h":"The column is too narrow to display the number or date","ok":1,"why":"widen the column"},{"h":"The cell is locked","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"<code>###</code> simply means the column needs to be widened."}]],"id":"office-07","title":"Microsoft Excel — Basics, formatting, and cell references","goal":"navigate workbooks and worksheets, format numbers, and distinguish relative ($A1$) from absolute ($A\\$1$) cell references","week":"8–9","minutes":18,"terms":[{"t":"cell reference","m":"a cell's coordinate such as `B3` or `$F$1`","tr":"hücre başvurusu"},{"t":"relative reference","m":"a reference (`A1`) that shifts automatically when copied","tr":"göreli başvuru"},{"t":"absolute reference","m":"a locked reference (`$A$1`) that never changes when copied","tr":"mutlak başvuru"},{"t":"fill handle","m":"the small square at the bottom-right of a selected cell used to copy formulas","tr":"doldurma tutamacı"}]},"office-08":{"html":"<p>Every Excel formula <strong>must start with <code>=</code></strong>. Without <code>=</code>, Excel treats what you typed as plain text!</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-essential-excel-functions\"><h2 id=\"essential-excel-functions\">Essential Excel functions</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>English</th><th>Turkish Excel</th><th>What it does</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>=SUM(A1:A5)</code></td><td><code>TOPLA</code></td><td>Adds numbers in a range</td><td><code>=SUM(B2:B6)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>=AVERAGE(A1:A5)</code></td><td><code>ORTALAMA</code></td><td>Arithmetic mean of numbers</td><td><code>=AVERAGE(B2:B6)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>=MIN(A1:A5)</code></td><td><code>MİN</code></td><td>Smallest number</td><td><code>=MIN(B2:B6)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>=MAX(A1:A5)</code></td><td><code>MAK</code></td><td>Largest number</td><td><code>=MAX(B2:B6)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>=COUNT(A1:A5)</code></td><td><code>BAĞ_DEĞ_SAY</code></td><td>Counts <strong>numeric</strong> cells only</td><td><code>=COUNT(B2:B6)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>=COUNTA(A1:A5)</code></td><td><code>BAĞ_DEĞ_DOLU_SAY</code></td><td>Counts <strong>all non-empty</strong> cells (text + numbers)</td><td><code>=COUNTA(A2:A6)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>=IF(cond, yes, no)</code></td><td><code>EĞER</code></td><td>Decision: returns <code>yes</code> if true, <code>no</code> if false</td><td><code>=IF(D2&gt;=60, \"Pass\", \"Fail\")</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>=COUNTIF(range, crit)</code></td><td><code>EĞERSAY</code></td><td>Counts cells matching a condition</td><td><code>=COUNTIF(E2:E6, \"Pass\")</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>=ROUND(num, digits)</code></td><td><code>YUVARLA</code></td><td>Rounds a number to <code>digits</code> decimals</td><td><code>=ROUND(C2, 2)</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><em>(Note: In Turkish-locale desktop Excel, arguments are separated by semicolons <code>;</code> instead of commas <code>,</code>—for example <code>=EĞER(D2&gt;=60; \"Geçti\"; \"Kaldı\")</code>.)</em></p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Use the interactive Excel formula sandbox below to complete the tasks (both English and Turkish names <code>TOPLA</code>, <code>ORTALAMA</code>, <code>EĞER</code> work!):</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"formula\"></div>\n<div class=\"widget checklist\" data-widget=\"checklist\" data-id=\"office/08-excel-formulas-functions.md#1\"><div class=\"checklist-h\">Lesson 8 hands-on checklist</div><ul class=\"checks\"><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"0\"><span>Completed all formula tasks in the interactive sandbox above</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"1\"><span>Tested <code>=SUM(...)</code>, <code>=AVERAGE(...)</code>, <code>=MIN(...)</code>, <code>=MAX(...)</code></span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"2\"><span>Wrote an <code>=IF(...)</code> condition with text results in double quotes (<code>\"Pass\"</code>)</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"3\"><span>Checked the difference between <code>COUNT</code> (numbers only) and <code>COUNTA</code> (all non-empty)</span></label></li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Forgetting the leading <strong><code>=</code></strong> sign (typing <code>SUM(A1:A5)</code> instead of <code>=SUM(A1:A5)</code>).</li><li>Writing text inside <code>IF</code> or <code>COUNTIF</code> without double quotes (<code>=IF(D2&gt;=60, Pass, Fail)</code> gives <code>#NAME?</code>—it must be <code>\"Pass\"</code>).</li><li>Confusing <code>COUNT</code> (ignores text!) with <code>COUNTA</code> (counts text and numbers).</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>formula</strong></td><td>an expression starting with <code>=</code> that computes a value in a spreadsheet</td><td lang=\"tr\">formül</td></tr><tr><td><strong><code>IF</code> (<code>EĞER</code>)</strong></td><td>conditional function returning one value if true and another if false</td><td lang=\"tr\">koşullu EĞER fonksiyonu</td></tr><tr><td><strong><code>COUNT</code> vs <code>COUNTA</code></strong></td><td><code>COUNT</code> counts numbers only; <code>COUNTA</code> counts all non-empty cells</td><td lang=\"tr\">SAY vs DOLU_SAY</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"Cells <code>A1:A4</code> contain <code>10</code>, <code>\"Ali\"</code>, <code>25</code>, and <em>(blank)</em>. What does <code>=COUNT(A1:A4)</code> return vs. <code>=COUNTA(A1:A4)</code>?","opts":[{"h":"<code>3</code> and <code>4</code>","why":"blank cell is not counted by <code>COUNTA</code>, and <code>\"Ali\"</code> is not counted by <code>COUNT</code>"},{"h":"<code>2</code> and <code>3</code>","ok":1,"why":"<code>COUNT</code> counts only the 2 numbers (<code>10, 25</code>); <code>COUNTA</code> counts the 3 non-empty cells (<code>10, \"Ali\", 25</code>)"},{"h":"<code>2</code> and <code>4</code>","why":"<code>COUNTA</code> skips blank cells"},{"h":"<code>4</code> and <code>4</code>","why":"<code>COUNT</code> skips text and blanks"}],"why":"<code>COUNT</code> counts numbers (<code>2</code>); <code>COUNTA</code> counts all non-empty cells (<code>3</code>)."},{"q":"Which formula returns <code>\"Pass\"</code> if cell <code>D2</code> is <code>60</code> or higher, and <code>\"Fail\"</code> otherwise?","opts":[{"h":"<code>IF(D2&gt;=60, \"Pass\", \"Fail\")</code>","why":"missing the leading <code>=</code>"},{"h":"<code>=IF(D2&gt;=60, \"Pass\", \"Fail\")</code>","ok":1,"why":"starts with <code>=</code>, checks <code>&gt;=60</code>, quotes text strings"},{"h":"<code>=IF(D2&gt;60, \"Pass\", \"Fail\")</code>","why":"<code>&gt;</code> excludes <code>60</code> itself"},{"h":"<code>=SUM(D2&gt;=60, \"Pass\", \"Fail\")</code>","why":"<code>SUM</code> adds numbers, not conditions"}],"why":"Start with <code>=</code>, use <code>&gt;= 60</code>, and wrap text outputs in double quotes."},{"q":"In Excel, what error appears if you write <code>=10/0</code> or divide by an empty cell?","opts":[{"h":"<code>#NAME?</code>","why":"<code>#NAME?</code> means misspelled function name or unquoted text"},{"h":"<code>#DIV/0!</code>","ok":1,"why":"division by zero error"},{"h":"<code>#VALUE!</code>","why":"wrong data type (e.g., adding text to a number)"},{"h":"<code>###</code>","why":"column too narrow"}],"why":"Dividing by zero produces <code>#DIV/0!</code>."}]],"id":"office-08","title":"Microsoft Excel — Essential formulas and functions","goal":"write Excel formulas using SUM, AVERAGE, MIN, MAX, COUNT, COUNTA, IF, COUNTIF, and ROUND (plus Turkish equivalents)","week":"10","minutes":22,"terms":[{"t":"formula","m":"an expression starting with `=` that computes a value in a spreadsheet","tr":"formül"},{"t":"`IF` (`EĞER`)","m":"conditional function returning one value if true and another if false","tr":"koşullu EĞER fonksiyonu"},{"t":"`COUNT` vs `COUNTA`","m":"`COUNT` counts numbers only; `COUNTA` counts all non-empty cells","tr":"SAY vs DOLU_SAY"}]},"office-09":{"html":"<p>Spreadsheets are not just for calculating numbers—they also help you <strong>organize</strong>, <strong>highlight</strong>, and <strong>visualize</strong> data.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-sorting-filtering\"><h2 id=\"sorting-filtering\">Sorting &amp; Filtering</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Sort</strong>: Click any cell inside your table → <code>Data → Sort &amp; Filter → Sort A to Z</code> / <code>Sort Z to A</code> / <code>Custom Sort</code> (multi-column sort, e.g., by Department then by Grade descending).</li><li><strong>Filter (AutoFilter)</strong>: Click inside your table → <code>Data → Sort &amp; Filter → Filter</code> (<code>Ctrl+Shift+L</code>). Drop-down arrows appear on every header so you can filter by value, text, or condition (<code>Greater Than...</code>).</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-conditional-formatting\"><h2 id=\"conditional-formatting\">Conditional Formatting</h2>\n<p>Automatically color cells based on their values (<code>Home → Styles → Conditional Formatting</code>):</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Highlight Cells Rules</strong>: e.g., mark grades <code>&lt; 60</code> in light red fill.</li><li><strong>Color Scales / Data Bars</strong>: show high vs. low values visually at a glance.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-choosing-the-right-chart-insert-charts\"><h2 id=\"choosing-the-right-chart-insert-charts\">Choosing the right chart (<code>Insert → Charts</code>)</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Chart type</th><th>Best used for</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Column / Bar</strong></td><td>Comparing categories side by side</td><td>Midterm averages by department</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Line</strong></td><td>Showing trends over <strong>time</strong></td><td>Monthly website visitors Jan–Dec</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Pie</strong></td><td>Showing <strong>parts of one whole</strong> (percentages summing to 100%)</td><td>Share of OS market (Windows, macOS, Linux)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-freeze-panes-print-setup\"><h2 id=\"freeze-panes-print-setup\">Freeze Panes &amp; Print Setup</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Keep header row visible while scrolling</strong>: <code>View → Window → Freeze Panes → Freeze Top Row</code>.</li><li><strong>Print cleanly</strong>: <code>Page Layout → Page Setup → Orientation (Landscape)</code> + <code>Scale to Fit → Width: 1 page</code>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<div class=\"widget checklist\" data-widget=\"checklist\" data-id=\"office/09-excel-charts-sort-filter.md#1\"><div class=\"checklist-h\">Lesson 9 hands-on checklist</div><ul class=\"checks\"><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"0\"><span>Turned on <strong>Filter</strong> (<code>Ctrl+Shift+L</code> or <code>Data → Filter</code>) on a multi-row table and filtered one category</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"1\"><span>Applied <strong>Conditional Formatting</strong> (<code>Home → Conditional Formatting → Highlight Cells Rules → Less Than</code>) to highlight scores below 60</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"2\"><span>Created a <strong>Column</strong> or <strong>Line</strong> chart (<code>Insert → Charts</code>) with a clear chart title</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"3\"><span>Froze the header row using <code>View → Freeze Panes → Freeze Top Row</code></span></label></li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Selecting <strong>only one column</strong> before clicking Sort—Excel either warns you or sorts that column alone, breaking the link between names and grades! Always click <strong>one cell inside the table</strong> (or select the whole table).</li><li>Using a <strong>Pie chart</strong> when values do not represent parts of one whole (or when there are 15 tiny slices)—use a <strong>Bar/Column chart</strong> instead.</li><li>Printing a 10-column Excel sheet without checking <strong>Print Preview</strong> (<code>Ctrl+P</code>), splitting the last 2 columns onto a separate orphan page.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>AutoFilter</strong></td><td>dropdown filters on table headers to show only matching rows (<code>Data → Filter</code>)</td><td lang=\"tr\">otomatik filtre</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Conditional Formatting</strong></td><td>formatting that changes cell color/style automatically based on cell values</td><td lang=\"tr\">koşullu biçimlendirme</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Freeze Panes</strong></td><td>locking header rows or columns so they stay visible while scrolling</td><td lang=\"tr\">bölmeleri dondur</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"Which chart type is best for showing how monthly sales changed from January to December?","opts":[{"h":"Pie chart","why":"Pie charts show shares of a single total, not time trends"},{"h":"Line chart","ok":1,"why":"Line charts clearly show trends over continuous time"},{"h":"Scatter plot","why":"Scatter plots compare two numeric variables"},{"h":"Radar chart","why":"hard to read for simple time series"}],"why":"Use a <strong>Line chart</strong> for trends over time."},{"q":"You want Row 1 (your column headers) to stay visible at the top while you scroll down through 500 student rows. Which menu path do you use?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Home → Wrap Text</code>","why":"wraps long text inside one cell"},{"h":"<code>Data → Filter</code>","why":"adds filter dropdowns, doesn't lock scrolling"},{"h":"<code>View → Freeze Panes → Freeze Top Row</code>","ok":1,"why":"locks Row 1 during scrolling"},{"h":"<code>Insert → Header &amp; Footer</code>","why":"only appears on printed pages"}],"why":"<code>View → Freeze Panes → Freeze Top Row</code> keeps Row 1 pinned on screen."},{"q":"What happens if you select <strong>only Column B</strong> (scores) and click Sort Largest to Smallest, ignoring Column A (names)?","opts":[{"h":"Excel always refuses to sort","why":"Excel may sort Column B alone if you choose \"Continue with current selection\""},{"h":"Scores get reordered while student names stay in place, mismatching every student's grade!","ok":1,"why":"always expand the selection or click one cell inside the table"},{"h":"Column A is deleted","why":"it stays, just mismatched"},{"h":"All formulas turn into <code>#REF!</code>","why":"values mismatch"}],"why":"Always select the whole table (or a single cell inside it) so rows stay together when sorting."}]],"id":"office-09","title":"Microsoft Excel — Sorting, filtering, conditional formatting, and charts","goal":"sort and filter tables cleanly, highlight rules with Conditional Formatting, and choose the right chart type","week":"10","minutes":18,"terms":[{"t":"AutoFilter","m":"dropdown filters on table headers to show only matching rows (`Data → Filter`)","tr":"otomatik filtre"},{"t":"Conditional Formatting","m":"formatting that changes cell color/style automatically based on cell values","tr":"koşullu biçimlendirme"},{"t":"Freeze Panes","m":"locking header rows or columns so they stay visible while scrolling","tr":"bölmeleri dondur"}]},"office-10":{"html":"<p>A clean presentation looks unified from Slide 1 to Slide 15. Instead of pasting a logo and changing fonts manually on every slide, PowerPoint gives you <strong>Slide Master</strong>.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-themes-layouts-and-slide-size\"><h2 id=\"themes-layouts-and-slide-size\">Themes, Layouts, and Slide Size</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Slide Size</strong>: <code>Design → Customize → Slide Size → Widescreen (16:9)</code> (modern standard for projectors and screens).</li><li><strong>Theme</strong>: <code>Design → Themes</code> sets coordinated colors, fonts, and backgrounds across the whole deck.</li><li><strong>Slide Layout</strong>: <code>Home → Slides → Layout</code> lets you pick <strong>Title Slide</strong>, <strong>Title and Content</strong>, <strong>Two Content</strong>, <strong>Comparison</strong>, or <strong>Blank</strong>. Always use built-in placeholders rather than drawing raw text boxes everywhere!</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-slide-master-view-master-views-slide-master\"><h2 id=\"slide-master-view-master-views-slide-master\">Slide Master (<code>View → Master Views → Slide Master</code>)</h2>\n<p><strong>Slide Master</strong> is the blueprint behind every slide:</p>\n<ul><li>Edit the <strong>top-most Master slide</strong> (the big slide at #1) to change the font, footer, or add a university logo to <strong>every</strong> slide at once!</li><li>Edit a <strong>child layout</strong> below it to customize only one layout (e.g., Title Slide).</li><li>Click <strong>Slide Master → Close Master View</strong> when finished so you don't accidentally write your presentation content inside the Master!</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-headers-footers-slide-numbers\"><h2 id=\"headers-footers-slide-numbers\">Headers, footers &amp; slide numbers</h2>\n<p><code>Insert → Text → Header &amp; Footer</code> → tick <strong>Slide number</strong> and <strong>Footer</strong> (e.g., course name) → tick <strong>Don't show on title slide</strong> → <strong>Apply to All</strong>.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<div class=\"widget checklist\" data-widget=\"checklist\" data-id=\"office/10-powerpoint-structure-master.md#1\"><div class=\"checklist-h\">Lesson 10 hands-on checklist</div><ul class=\"checks\"><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"0\"><span>Confirmed slide size is <strong>16:9 Widescreen</strong> (<code>Design → Slide Size</code>)</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"1\"><span>Opened <code>View → Slide Master</code>, placed a small logo or accent bar on the top Master slide, then clicked <strong>Close Master View</strong></span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"2\"><span>Added slide numbers via <code>Insert → Header &amp; Footer</code> with <strong>Don't show on title slide</strong> checked</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"3\"><span>Created 3 slides using built-in <strong>Layouts</strong> (<code>Title Slide</code>, <code>Title and Content</code>, <code>Two Content</code>)</span></label></li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Typing actual presentation text while still inside <strong>Slide Master</strong> view—every new slide then inherits that text! Always click <strong>Close Master View</strong> first.</li><li>Pasting a university logo onto 20 slides one by one instead of placing it once on the <strong>Slide Master</strong>.</li><li>Using <code>4:3</code> Standard on a modern <code>16:9</code> classroom projector (leaves black bars on both sides).</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Slide Master</strong></td><td>the template blueprint (<code>View → Slide Master</code>) controlling fonts, logos, and layouts across all slides</td><td lang=\"tr\">asıl slayt</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Slide Layout</strong></td><td>a predefined arrangement of title, text, and media placeholders (<code>Home → Layout</code>)</td><td lang=\"tr\">slayt düzeni</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Theme</strong></td><td>a coordinated set of colors, fonts, and effects (<code>Design → Themes</code>)</td><td lang=\"tr\">tema</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"You want your university logo to appear in the exact same top-right corner on <strong>every</strong> slide without copying it 20 times. Where should you place it?","opts":[{"h":"On Slide 1 only","why":"it will only appear on Slide 1"},{"h":"On the top-level slide in <code>View → Slide Master</code>","ok":1,"why":"changes on the top Master slide apply across all layouts"},{"h":"Inside Notes Page view","why":"Notes view is for speaker notes"},{"h":"Inside Slide Sorter view","why":"Slide Sorter reorders slides"}],"why":"Place global logos, fonts, and footers on the top Slide Master."},{"q":"Which menu path adds slide numbers while hiding the number on Slide 1 (the title slide)?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Design → Format Background</code>","why":"changes slide background"},{"h":"<code>Insert → Header &amp; Footer</code> → check <strong>Slide number</strong> and <strong>Don't show on title slide</strong> → <strong>Apply to All</strong>","ok":1,"why":"standard path"},{"h":"<code>View → Reading View</code>","why":"preview mode"},{"h":"<code>Animations → Add Animation</code>","why":"animations are for object motion"}],"why":"<code>Insert → Header &amp; Footer</code> controls slide numbers, footers, and title-slide suppression."},{"q":"What is the most common mistake students make after editing <code>View → Slide Master</code>?","opts":[{"h":"Saving as <code>.pptx</code>","why":"<code>.pptx</code> is the normal format"},{"h":"Forgetting to click <strong>Close Master View</strong> and typing slide content directly into the master layouts","ok":1,"why":"puts their text onto the template itself"},{"h":"Using 16:9 widescreen","why":"16:9 is recommended"},{"h":"Applying a Theme","why":"Themes are designed to be applied"}],"why":"Always click <strong>Close Master View</strong> before authoring individual slides."}]],"id":"office-10","title":"Microsoft PowerPoint — Slide Master, themes, and layouts","goal":"structure a 16:9 presentation consistently using Themes, Slide Layouts, and Slide Master","week":"11, 13","minutes":16,"terms":[{"t":"Slide Master","m":"the template blueprint (`View → Slide Master`) controlling fonts, logos, and layouts across all slides","tr":"asıl slayt"},{"t":"Slide Layout","m":"a predefined arrangement of title, text, and media placeholders (`Home → Layout`)","tr":"slayt düzeni"},{"t":"Theme","m":"a coordinated set of colors, fonts, and effects (`Design → Themes`)","tr":"tema"}]},"office-11":{"html":"<p>Slides are <strong>visual aids</strong> for your audience, not a Word document projected onto a wall. If the audience is reading paragraphs on your slide, they stop listening to you!</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-golden-rules-of-slide-design\"><h2 id=\"golden-rules-of-slide-design\">Golden rules of slide design</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>The 6×6 rule</strong>: aim for at most <strong>6 bullets per slide</strong> and <strong>6 words per bullet</strong> (keywords, not full sentences).</li><li><strong>Readable font sizes</strong>: Titles <strong>32–44 pt</strong>, body text <strong>20–28 pt</strong> (never below 18 pt!). Use clean sans-serif fonts (Calibri, Arial, Segoe UI).</li><li><strong>High contrast</strong>: dark text on a light background (safest in bright classrooms) or crisp white text on a deep dark background. Never put yellow text on white or dark blue text on black!</li><li><strong>One idea per slide</strong>: split dense topics across two slides rather than shrinking text to 12 pt.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-smartart-tables-charts\"><h2 id=\"smartart-tables-charts\">SmartArt, Tables &amp; Charts</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>SmartArt</strong> (<code>Insert → Illustrations → SmartArt</code>): turns plain bullet lists into <strong>Process</strong> arrows, <strong>Hierarchy</strong> org charts, or <strong>Cycle</strong> diagrams. (You can also right-click an existing bullet list → <strong>Convert to SmartArt</strong>!)</li><li><strong>Tables &amp; Charts</strong>: <code>Insert → Table</code> or <code>Insert → Chart</code>. If you copy a chart from Excel, <strong>Paste → Keep Source Formatting &amp; Link Data</strong> updates the slide chart automatically if the Excel numbers change!</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-designer-design-ideas\"><h2 id=\"designer-design-ideas\">Designer (Design Ideas)</h2>\n<p><strong>Design → Designer</strong> (called <em>Design Ideas</em> in older versions) suggests professional layouts for the current slide when you insert a picture, a list or a chart. Click a thumbnail to apply it. It needs an internet connection and a Microsoft 365 subscription.</p>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<div class=\"widget checklist\" data-widget=\"checklist\" data-id=\"office/11-powerpoint-visuals-tables.md#1\"><div class=\"checklist-h\">Lesson 11 hands-on checklist</div><ul class=\"checks\"><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"0\"><span>Converted a 4-item process list into <strong>SmartArt</strong> (<code>Home → Convert to SmartArt</code> or <code>Insert → SmartArt</code>)</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"1\"><span>Checked every slide's body font size is <strong>at least 20 pt</strong> with strong text/background contrast</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"2\"><span>Trimmed a wordy paragraph down to short <strong>6×6</strong> keyword bullets</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"3\"><span>Inserted one clean table or chart (<code>Insert → Chart</code>) with a descriptive title</span></label></li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Pasting whole paragraphs from Wikipedia onto a slide in 12 pt font and reading them aloud word for word.</li><li>Using low-contrast backgrounds (busy photos behind text without a dark/light overlay box).</li><li>Stretching images by dragging only the <strong>side</strong> handle instead of a <strong>corner</strong> handle (distorts faces and logos!).</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>6×6 rule</strong></td><td>guideline of at most 6 bullets per slide and 6 words per bullet</td><td lang=\"tr\">6×6 kuralı</td></tr><tr><td><strong>SmartArt</strong></td><td>built-in visual diagrams (Process, Hierarchy, Cycle) for structured ideas</td><td lang=\"tr\">SmartArt grafiği</td></tr><tr><td><strong>contrast</strong></td><td>visual difference between text color and background color for readability</td><td lang=\"tr\">kontrast</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"What does the <strong>6×6 rule</strong> in PowerPoint recommend?","opts":[{"h":"6 slides total with 6 transitions each","why":"transitions should be minimal"},{"h":"At most ~6 bullet points per slide and ~6 words per bullet","ok":1,"why":"keeps slides scannable instead of walls of text"},{"h":"6 colors and 6 fonts per slide","why":"use at most 2 fonts and a small palette"},{"h":"6-minute presentation at 6 pm","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"The 6×6 rule prevents text-heavy, unreadable slides."},{"q":"How should you resize a photo or logo on a slide so it does <strong>not</strong> look stretched or squashed?","opts":[{"h":"Drag the top edge handle","why":"distorts height only"},{"h":"Drag the right edge handle","why":"distorts width only"},{"h":"Drag a <strong>corner</strong> handle (or hold <code>Shift</code> if needed)","ok":1,"why":"corner handles preserve aspect ratio"},{"h":"Change the slide size","why":"changes the whole deck"}],"why":"Always resize images from a <strong>corner</strong> handle to keep proportions intact."},{"q":"Which PowerPoint feature converts a plain bulleted process list into a visual diagram in one click?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Design → Variants</code>","why":"changes theme colors"},{"h":"<code>Home → Paragraph → Convert to SmartArt</code>","ok":1,"why":"turns bullets directly into SmartArt diagrams"},{"h":"<code>Transitions → Morph</code>","why":"slide-to-slide transition"},{"h":"<code>Review → Compare</code>","why":"compares two decks"}],"why":"Convert to SmartArt turns text lists into diagrams immediately."}]],"id":"office-11","title":"Microsoft PowerPoint — Visuals, SmartArt, and slide design","goal":"apply readable slide design rules (contrast, typography, 6x6 rule) and insert SmartArt, tables, and Excel charts","week":"11","minutes":15,"terms":[{"t":"6×6 rule","m":"guideline of at most 6 bullets per slide and 6 words per bullet","tr":"6×6 kuralı"},{"t":"SmartArt","m":"built-in visual diagrams (Process, Hierarchy, Cycle) for structured ideas","tr":"SmartArt grafiği"},{"t":"contrast","m":"visual difference between text color and background color for readability","tr":"kontrast"}]},"office-12":{"html":"<p>Motion in PowerPoint should guide the audience's eye—never distract them.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-transitions-vs-animations\"><h2 id=\"transitions-vs-animations\">Transitions vs. Animations</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Applies to</th><th>Ribbon tab</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Transition</strong></td><td>How <strong>one slide</strong> changes to the <strong>next slide</strong></td><td><code>Transitions</code></td><td><code>Fade</code>, <code>Push</code>, <code>Morph</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Animation</strong></td><td>How <strong>objects on a slide</strong> (bullets, charts) appear, emphasize, or exit</td><td><code>Animations</code></td><td><code>Appear</code>, <code>Fade</code>, <code>Fly In</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-controlling-animations-cleanly\"><h2 id=\"controlling-animations-cleanly\">Controlling animations cleanly</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Effect Options</strong>: e.g., reveal bullet points <strong>By Paragraph</strong> on click so the audience doesn't read ahead.</li><li><strong>Animation Pane</strong> (<code>Animations → Advanced Animation → Animation Pane</code>): shows the exact order and timing (<code>On Click</code>, <code>With Previous</code>, <code>After Previous</code>).</li><li><strong>Consistency</strong>: pick <strong>one</strong> subtle transition (like <code>Fade</code>) and click <strong>Transitions → Timing → Apply to All</strong>—never use 15 spinning/shattering transitions!</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-media-presenter-view\"><h2 id=\"media-presenter-view\">Media &amp; Presenter View</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Video / Audio</strong>: <code>Insert → Media → Video / Audio</code> (prefer local files embedded in the <code>.pptx</code> rather than fragile internet links during classroom talks!).</li><li><strong>Speaker Notes &amp; Presenter View</strong>: type talking points in the <strong>Notes</strong> pane below the slide. During a talk (<code>Slide Show → Use Presenter View</code>), the projector shows only the clean slide while your laptop screen shows your notes, timer, and next slide!</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<div class=\"widget checklist\" data-widget=\"checklist\" data-id=\"office/12-powerpoint-animations-media.md#1\"><div class=\"checklist-h\">Lesson 12 hands-on checklist</div><ul class=\"checks\"><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"0\"><span>Applied one subtle <strong>Transition</strong> (<code>Transitions → Fade → Apply to All</code>)</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"1\"><span>Added an <strong>Entrance</strong> animation (<code>Appear</code> or <code>Fade</code>) to a bullet list and opened <strong>Animation Pane</strong> to verify <code>On Click</code> order</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"2\"><span>Typed 2–3 talking points in the <strong>Notes</strong> pane at the bottom of a slide</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"3\"><span>Tested <strong>Slide Show → From Beginning</strong> (<code>F5</code>) and <strong>From Current Slide</strong> (<code>Shift+F5</code>)</span></label></li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Using noisy or slow 3-second animations (<code>Bounce</code>, <code>Spin</code>) on every heading—wastes time and looks unprofessional.</li><li>Linking to a YouTube video when the classroom projector PC has no Wi-Fi—always embed local MP4/audio or have a backup!</li><li>Putting your entire speech onto the slide instead of the <strong>Notes</strong> pane.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>transition</strong></td><td>visual effect when moving from one slide to the next</td><td lang=\"tr\">slayt geçişi</td></tr><tr><td><strong>animation</strong></td><td>visual effect applied to an individual object on a slide</td><td lang=\"tr\">animasyon</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Animation Pane</strong></td><td>sidebar listing all animations on the current slide and their timing</td><td lang=\"tr\">animasyon bölmesi</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Presenter View</strong></td><td>dual-screen mode showing speaker notes and timer to the presenter only</td><td lang=\"tr\">sunucu görünümü</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"What is the difference between a <strong>Transition</strong> and an <strong>Animation</strong> in PowerPoint?","opts":[{"h":"They are two names for the same effect","why":"transitions are between slides; animations are on objects"},{"h":"A <strong>Transition</strong> happens between slides; an <strong>Animation</strong> moves or reveals individual objects on a slide","ok":1,"why":"e.g., Fade between slides vs. bullets appearing one by one"},{"h":"Transitions only work on Title Slides","why":"transitions work on any slide"},{"h":"Animations cannot be clicked","why":"<code>On Click</code> is the default animation trigger"}],"why":"Transitions = slide-to-slide; Animations = objects within a slide."},{"q":"Which keyboard shortcut starts Slide Show <strong>from the very first slide</strong>, and which starts <strong>from the current slide</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"<code>F1</code> and <code>F2</code>","why":"Help and Rename"},{"h":"<code>F5</code> (from beginning) and <code>Shift+F5</code> (from current slide)","ok":1,"why":"essential presenter shortcuts"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+S</code> and <code>Ctrl+P</code>","why":"Save and Print"},{"h":"<code>Alt+F4</code> and <code>Esc</code>","why":"Close and Exit"}],"why":"<code>F5</code> starts from Slide 1; <code>Shift+F5</code> starts from the current slide."},{"q":"Where should you put detailed talking points so <strong>you</strong> can read them on your laptop during <strong>Presenter View</strong> while the audience only sees clean slides?","opts":[{"h":"Inside a tiny text box in the corner","why":"audience sees it on the projector"},{"h":"In the <strong>Notes</strong> pane below the slide","ok":1,"why":"Presenter View shows Notes only on your screen"},{"h":"In Slide Master","why":"shows on every slide to the audience"},{"h":"In the file properties","why":"not visible during Slide Show"}],"why":"Use the <strong>Notes</strong> pane + <strong>Presenter View</strong> for speaker prompts."}]],"id":"office-12","title":"Microsoft PowerPoint — Transitions, animations, and media","goal":"distinguish slide transitions from object animations, control timing with the Animation Pane, and embed media and speaker notes","week":"12","minutes":16,"terms":[{"t":"transition","m":"visual effect when moving from one slide to the next","tr":"slayt geçişi"},{"t":"animation","m":"visual effect applied to an individual object on a slide","tr":"animasyon"},{"t":"Animation Pane","m":"sidebar listing all animations on the current slide and their timing","tr":"animasyon bölmesi"},{"t":"Presenter View","m":"dual-screen mode showing speaker notes and timer to the presenter only","tr":"sunucu görünümü"}]},"office-13":{"html":"<p>Great slides still fail if fonts break on the classroom PC or you run out of time. Here is how to finish and deliver cleanly.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-rehearsing-slide-show-shortcuts\"><h2 id=\"rehearsing-slide-show-shortcuts\">Rehearsing &amp; Slide Show shortcuts</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Rehearse Timings</strong> (<code>Slide Show → Set Up → Rehearse Timings</code>): practices your talk with a live timer per slide.</li><li><strong>Live Slide Show shortcuts</strong>: - <code>N</code> / <code>Space</code> / <code>→</code> : Next slide or animation - <code>P</code> / <code>←</code> : Previous - <code>B</code> : Black screen (pauses audience attention on you!) · <code>W</code> : White screen - <code>Ctrl+P</code> : Pen tool to draw/highlight live on a slide (<code>E</code> erases) - <code>Esc</code> : End Slide Show</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-exporting-sharing-safely\"><h2 id=\"exporting-sharing-safely\">Exporting &amp; sharing safely</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Export as PDF</strong> (<code>File → Export → Create PDF/XPS</code>): <strong>never</strong> shifts fonts or layouts, even on Linux/Mac classroom PCs! Always keep a PDF backup on your USB/cloud.</li><li><strong>Print Handouts</strong> (<code>File → Print → Full Page Slides</code> → change to <code>3 Slides</code> or <code>6 Slides Horizontal</code>): prints multiple slides per page (with note lines on <code>3 Slides</code>).</li><li><strong>Export as Video</strong> (<code>File → Export → Create a Video</code>): turns a timed/narrated deck into an <code>.mp4</code>.</li><li><strong>Embed fonts</strong> (<code>File → Options → Save → Embed fonts in the file</code>): protects custom <code>.pptx</code> fonts when opening on another Windows PC.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<div class=\"widget checklist\" data-widget=\"checklist\" data-id=\"office/13-presenting-and-export.md#1\"><div class=\"checklist-h\">Lesson 13 hands-on checklist</div><ul class=\"checks\"><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"0\"><span>Started Slide Show (<code>F5</code>) and tested pressing <code>B</code> (black screen) and <code>Ctrl+P</code> (pen highlight)</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"1\"><span>Exported a deck to <strong>PDF</strong> (<code>File → Export → Create PDF/XPS</code>) as a safe backup</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"2\"><span>Checked <code>File → Print → Settings</code> and switched from <code>Full Page Slides</code> to <code>3 Slides</code> handout view</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"3\"><span>Checked <code>Slide Show → Rehearse Timings</code></span></label></li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-common-mistakes\"><h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common mistakes</h2>\n<ul><li>Bringing only a <code>.pptx</code> using a downloaded custom font—on the lab PC, PowerPoint substitutes Arial and overflows text boxes! Always <strong>embed fonts</strong> or bring a <strong>PDF</strong> backup.</li><li>Pressing <code>Esc</code> instead of <code>B</code> when you want the audience to look at you during a discussion—<code>Esc</code> exposes your messy PowerPoint editing window.</li><li>Reading slides with your back turned to the audience instead of facing them and glancing at Presenter View.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-key-terms\"><h2 id=\"key-terms\">Key terms</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table class=\"terms\"><thead><tr><th>English term</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Turkish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Rehearse Timings</strong></td><td>Slide Show tool that measures how long you spend on each slide</td><td lang=\"tr\">zamanlama provası</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Handouts</strong></td><td>multi-slide-per-page print layout (<code>3 Slides</code>, <code>6 Slides</code>)</td><td lang=\"tr\">dinleyici notları</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Embed fonts</strong></td><td>saving font files inside <code>.pptx</code> so text looks identical on other PCs</td><td lang=\"tr\">yazı tiplerini gömme</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-quick-check\"><h2 id=\"quick-check\">Quick check</h2>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"quiz\" data-k=\"0\"></div>\n</section>","quizzes":[[{"q":"During a live PowerPoint Slide Show, which key turns the projector screen <strong>black</strong> so the audience focuses on you?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Esc</code>","why":"exits Slide Show into the editor"},{"h":"<code>B</code>","ok":1,"why":"toggles a solid black screen (<code>B</code> again resumes)"},{"h":"<code>F5</code>","why":"restarts Slide Show"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+S</code>","why":"saves"}],"why":"Press <code>B</code> for black screen (or <code>W</code> for white screen) during a live talk."},{"q":"You designed a <code>.pptx</code> at home with a custom font and will present on an unfamiliar university lab PC. What is the safest way to guarantee your layout never breaks?","opts":[{"h":"Delete all titles","why":"unhelpful"},{"h":"Export a <strong>PDF</strong> backup (<code>File → Export → Create PDF/XPS</code>) and/or enable <strong>Embed fonts</strong> in <code>.pptx</code>","ok":1,"why":"PDF locks exact layout on any computer"},{"h":"Save as <code>.txt</code>","why":"loses slides and images"},{"h":"Turn off Slide Master","why":"doesn't protect fonts"}],"why":"Always bring a PDF backup (and embed fonts in <code>.pptx</code>)."},{"q":"Which Print layout prints <strong>3 slides per page</strong> with blank lines beside each slide for audience notes?","opts":[{"h":"Full Page Slides","why":"1 slide per page, no note lines"},{"h":"<code>3 Slides</code> (under Handouts)","ok":1,"why":"standard PowerPoint note-taking handout layout"},{"h":"Outline","why":"text only, no slide thumbnails"},{"h":"Notes Pages","why":"1 slide + presenter notes per page"}],"why":"The <code>3 Slides</code> handout layout includes writing lines next to each thumbnail."}]],"id":"office-13","title":"Presenting, rehearsing, and exporting presentations","goal":"rehearse presentation timing, package fonts/media safely, and export PowerPoint decks to PDF, handouts, and video","week":"14","minutes":14,"terms":[{"t":"Rehearse Timings","m":"Slide Show tool that measures how long you spend on each slide","tr":"zamanlama provası"},{"t":"Handouts","m":"multi-slide-per-page print layout (`3 Slides`, `6 Slides`)","tr":"dinleyici notları"},{"t":"Embed fonts","m":"saving font files inside `.pptx` so text looks identical on other PCs","tr":"yazı tiplerini gömme"}]},"office-14":{"html":"<p>This final Office Applications lab brings together <strong>Excel formulas</strong>, <strong>Word reporting</strong>, and <strong>PowerPoint slides</strong>—the exact workflow you will use across university projects.</p>\n<section class=\"sec sec-part-1-excel-formula-lab\"><h2 id=\"part-1-excel-formula-lab\">Part 1: Excel formula lab</h2>\n<p>Test your <code>SUM</code>, <code>AVERAGE</code>, <code>IF</code>, <code>ROUND</code>, and absolute reference skills in the interactive sandbox:</p>\n<div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"formula\"></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-part-2-complete-mini-project-workflow\"><h2 id=\"part-2-complete-mini-project-workflow\">Part 2: Complete mini-project workflow</h2>\n<ol><li><strong>Excel</strong>: Build a 5-student grade sheet (<code>Name</code>, <code>Midterm</code>, <code>Final</code>, <code>Weighted Avg = 0.4*Mid + 0.6*Fin</code>, <code>Status = IF(Avg&gt;=60, \"Pass\", \"Fail\")</code>), add <code>AVERAGE</code>/<code>MAX</code>/<code>MIN</code>, and insert a <strong>Column Chart</strong>.</li><li><strong>Word</strong>: Write a 2-page summary report using <strong>Heading 1 / Heading 2</strong> styles, an automatic <strong>Table of Contents</strong>, a pasted table/chart with <strong>Insert Caption</strong>, and export to <strong><code>.pdf</code></strong>.</li><li><strong>PowerPoint</strong>: Build a 4-slide <strong>16:9</strong> summary deck with a <strong>Slide Master</strong> footer, <strong>6×6</strong> bullets, the Excel chart, and export a <strong><code>.pdf</code></strong> backup.</li></ol>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-try-it\"><h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<div class=\"widget checklist\" data-widget=\"checklist\" data-id=\"office/14-mixed-hands-on-tasks.md#1\"><div class=\"checklist-h\">Final Office Applications readiness checklist</div><ul class=\"checks\"><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"0\"><span>Completed every task in the Excel <code>@widget formula</code> sandbox above</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"1\"><span>Built a Word report with Heading styles + automatic Table of Contents + PDF export</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"2\"><span>Built a 16:9 PowerPoint deck with Slide Master + clean chart + Presenter Notes</span></label></li><li><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-i=\"3\"><span>Practiced keyboard shortcuts (<code>Ctrl+H</code>, <code>Ctrl+Enter</code>, <code>F4</code>, <code>F5</code>, <code>Shift+F5</code>, <code>Ctrl+Shift+L</code>)</span></label></li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-next-steps\"><h2 id=\"next-steps\">Next steps</h2>\n<ul><li>Review the <a href=\"#/cheatsheet/office\">Office Cheat Sheet</a> and shortcut flashcards.</li><li>Take the timed <a href=\"#/mock/office/midterm\">Office Midterm Mock</a> (30 questions, 45 min) and <a href=\"#/mock/office/final\">Office Final Mock</a> (40 questions, 60 min).</li></ul>\n</section>","id":"office-14","title":"Mixed hands-on Office lab (Word + Excel + PowerPoint)","goal":"combine Word, Excel, and PowerPoint skills in a realistic end-of-course mini-project","week":"15","minutes":25}},"bank":[{"q":"Which Google search operator restricts results to a single domain such as <code>.edu.tr</code>?","opts":[{"h":"<code>filetype:</code>","why":"filters by file extension (e.g., <code>pdf</code>)"},{"h":"<code>site:</code>","ok":1,"why":"<code>site:edu.tr</code> searches only within <code>.edu.tr</code> domains"},{"h":"<code>inurl:</code>","why":"matches URL text, not strictly the domain"},{"h":"<code>-</code>","why":"excludes a keyword"}],"why":"Use <code>site:edu.tr</code> to limit search results to Turkish university domains.","tag":"01"},{"q":"Which search query finds the exact phrase <code>computer networks</code> in PDF format while excluding the word <code>cisco</code>?","opts":[{"h":"<code>computer networks pdf -cisco</code>","why":"does not require exact phrase or PDF filetype"},{"h":"<code>\"computer networks\" filetype:pdf -cisco</code>","ok":1,"why":"quotes force exact phrase, <code>filetype:pdf</code> filters format, <code>-cisco</code> excludes"},{"h":"<code>site:pdf \"computer networks\"</code>","why":"<code>site:</code> expects a domain, not a file type"},{"h":"<code>\"computer networks\" +pdf</code>","why":"<code>+</code> does not filter by file extension"}],"why":"Combine <code>\"...\"</code>, <code>filetype:pdf</code>, and <code>-word</code> for targeted academic searches.","tag":"01"},{"q":"When sending an announcement to 50 students who do not know each other, where should you put their email addresses?","opts":[{"h":"<code>To</code>","why":"exposes everyone's email address"},{"h":"<code>CC</code>","why":"exposes everyone's email address"},{"h":"<code>BCC</code>","ok":1,"why":"hides recipients' addresses from one another"},{"h":"<code>Reply-To</code>","why":"sets where replies go"}],"why":"Always use BCC for group announcements to protect privacy.","tag":"01"},{"q":"What does <strong>CC</strong> stand for in email?","opts":[{"h":"Central Copy","why":"incorrect"},{"h":"Carbon Copy","ok":1,"why":"visible copy sent to people who should stay informed"},{"h":"Closed Copy","why":"incorrect"},{"h":"Cloud Copy","why":"incorrect"}],"why":"CC = Carbon Copy (recipients are visible to all).","tag":"01"},{"q":"A company sells cloud accounting software to other businesses. Which e-commerce model is this?","opts":[{"h":"B2C","why":"business to individual consumer"},{"h":"B2B","ok":1,"why":"Business-to-Business"},{"h":"C2C","why":"consumer to consumer"},{"h":"C2B","why":"consumer to business"}],"why":"Business selling products or services to another business is B2B.","tag":"01"},{"q":"An individual sells a second-hand laptop to another individual on an online marketplace. Which model is this?","opts":[{"h":"B2B","why":"business to business"},{"h":"B2C","why":"business to consumer"},{"h":"C2C","ok":1,"why":"Consumer-to-Consumer"},{"h":"G2C","why":"government to citizen"}],"why":"Person-to-person sales via a platform are C2C.","tag":"01"},{"q":"A freelance designer sells custom icons to a software company. Which e-commerce model best describes this?","opts":[{"h":"B2B","why":"two companies"},{"h":"B2C","why":"company selling to consumer"},{"h":"C2C","why":"two consumers"},{"h":"C2B","ok":1,"why":"Consumer-to-Business (individual providing value to a business)"}],"why":"An individual offering goods or services to a business is C2B.","tag":"01"},{"q":"Which email subject line is <strong>most professional</strong> when asking a professor about a lab grade?","opts":[{"h":"<code>help urgent</code>","why":"vague, no course or topic"},{"h":"<code>(no subject)</code>","why":"unprofessional and easily missed"},{"h":"<code>CMP151 Sec 1 — Question on Lab 4 Grade</code>","ok":1,"why":"clear course, section, and topic"},{"h":"<code>Can you check my grade please because I think there is a mistake on question 3</code>","why":"way too long for a subject line"}],"why":"A good subject line is concise and includes the course code and topic.","tag":"01"},{"q":"What does the minus sign (<code>-</code>) do in a Google search like <code>java -coffee</code>?","opts":[{"h":"Searches only for <code>coffee</code>","why":"opposite"},{"h":"Excludes results containing the word <code>coffee</code>","ok":1,"why":"keeps results focused on Java programming"},{"h":"Searches for exact phrase <code>\"java coffee\"</code>","why":"quotes do exact phrase"},{"h":"Forces PDF results","why":"<code>filetype:pdf</code> does that"}],"why":"Prefixing a word with <code>-</code> (no space) removes pages containing that word.","tag":"01"},{"q":"Which file extension produces a <strong>fixed-layout</strong> document that looks identical across Windows, Mac, Linux, and phones?","opts":[{"h":"<code>.docx</code>","why":"fonts/spacing can shift if fonts are missing"},{"h":"<code>.txt</code>","why":"unformatted plain text"},{"h":"<code>.pdf</code>","ok":1,"why":"Portable Document Format preserves exact layout"},{"h":"<code>.csv</code>","why":"comma-separated table data"}],"why":"Always export final reports and CVs as <code>.pdf</code> when layout matters.","tag":"02"},{"q":"Which file extension stores a spreadsheet workbook created in Microsoft Excel?","opts":[{"h":"<code>.docx</code>","why":"Word document"},{"h":"<code>.xlsx</code>","ok":1,"why":"Excel workbook"},{"h":"<code>.pptx</code>","why":"PowerPoint presentation"},{"h":"<code>.zip</code>","why":"compressed archive"}],"why":"<code>.xlsx</code> is the standard Microsoft Excel workbook extension.","tag":"02"},{"q":"You need to submit 5 separate <code>.c</code> source files through a portal that only allows <strong>1 file</strong> upload. What should you do?","opts":[{"h":"Paste all 5 into a <code>.pptx</code>","why":"wrong format"},{"h":"Compress the folder into a single <code>.zip</code> archive","ok":1,"why":"bundles multiple files into one uploadable file"},{"h":"Rename the folder to <code>.pdf</code>","why":"renaming a folder does not make a valid PDF"},{"h":"Delete 4 of the files","why":"loses work"}],"why":"Compress multiple files/folders into a <code>.zip</code> archive.","tag":"02"},{"q":"What is a <code>.csv</code> file?","opts":[{"h":"A compressed PowerPoint","why":"<code>.pptx</code> / <code>.zip</code>"},{"h":"A plain-text table where columns are separated by commas","ok":1,"why":"easily opened in Excel, Python, or SQL tools"},{"h":"An encrypted PDF","why":"<code>.pdf</code>"},{"h":"A Word macro template","why":"<code>.dotm</code>"}],"why":"CSV stands for Comma-Separated Values.","tag":"02"},{"q":"Why is it good practice to enable <strong>File name extensions</strong> in Windows File Explorer?","opts":[{"h":"It makes files smaller","why":"display setting only"},{"h":"You can immediately verify the true file type (e.g., <code>.pdf</code> vs <code>.docx</code> vs <code>.exe</code>)","ok":1,"why":"prevents submitting shortcuts or opening disguised executables"},{"h":"It automatically backs up to OneDrive","why":"unrelated"},{"h":"It enables Track Changes","why":"Word feature"}],"why":"Seeing file extensions prevents format mix-ups and improves security awareness.","tag":"02"},{"q":"You share a Google Drive folder of lecture slides with classmates and want them to download slides <strong>without</strong> deleting or editing them. Which role should you assign?","opts":[{"h":"Viewer","ok":1,"why":"read and download only"},{"h":"Commenter","why":"can add comments"},{"h":"Editor","why":"can edit and delete files"},{"h":"Owner","why":"transfers full ownership"}],"why":"Assign <strong>Viewer</strong> for read-only sharing.","tag":"02"},{"q":"Which Google Drive permission allows a teammate to propose comments on a document without directly overwriting the body text?","opts":[{"h":"Viewer","why":"cannot comment"},{"h":"Commenter","ok":1,"why":"can add comments/suggestions without editing original text directly"},{"h":"Editor","why":"edits directly"},{"h":"Restricted","why":"blocks access"}],"why":"Commenter lets reviewers leave feedback safely.","tag":"02"},{"q":"What is the native editable file extension for Microsoft PowerPoint?","opts":[{"h":"<code>.docx</code>","why":"Word"},{"h":"<code>.xlsx</code>","why":"Excel"},{"h":"<code>.pptx</code>","ok":1,"why":"PowerPoint presentation"},{"h":"<code>.pdf</code>","why":"exported fixed document"}],"why":"<code>.pptx</code> is the modern XML-based PowerPoint extension.","tag":"02"},{"q":"In Google Docs, which mode marks your edits as colored suggestions for teammates to accept or reject?","opts":[{"h":"Editing","why":"changes text immediately without review prompts"},{"h":"Suggesting","ok":1,"why":"proposes insertions/deletions for approval"},{"h":"Viewing","why":"read-only"},{"h":"Offline","why":"local cache mode"}],"why":"Suggesting mode is Google Docs' equivalent of Track Changes.","tag":"03"},{"q":"How can you restore yesterday's version of a Google Doc after accidental deletions?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Tools → Spelling</code>","why":"checks spelling"},{"h":"<code>File → Version history → See version history</code>","ok":1,"why":"lets you view and restore earlier snapshots"},{"h":"<code>Insert → Bookmark</code>","why":"adds internal link"},{"h":"<code>Format → Clear formatting</code>","why":"strips styles"}],"why":"Version history keeps timestamped revisions you can restore.","tag":"03"},{"q":"Where do you click in <strong>Google Forms</strong> to send all survey answers automatically into a live spreadsheet?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Questions → Add section</code>","why":"splits the form into pages"},{"h":"<code>Responses → Link to Sheets</code>","ok":1,"why":"creates/links a Google Sheet collecting every submission"},{"h":"<code>Settings → Presentation</code>","why":"edits confirmation message"},{"h":"<code>Send → Embed HTML</code>","why":"embeds form on a website"}],"why":"<code>Responses → Link to Sheets</code> streams all form answers into Google Sheets.","tag":"03"},{"q":"In Google Forms, what does toggling <strong>Required</strong> on a question do?","opts":[{"h":"Makes the question worth 10 points","why":"quiz point values are set in Answer Key"},{"h":"Prevents the user from submitting the form without answering that question","ok":1,"why":"avoids missing Student IDs or names"},{"h":"Hides the question from mobile users","why":"displays on all devices"},{"h":"Converts the form to a PDF","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"<strong>Required</strong> enforces non-empty answers before submission.","tag":"03"},{"q":"Which Google Workspace tool lets you build a simple multi-page course portfolio or project website without writing HTML?","opts":[{"h":"Google Sheets","why":"spreadsheets"},{"h":"Google Forms","why":"surveys/quizzes"},{"h":"Google Sites","ok":1,"why":"drag-and-drop website builder"},{"h":"Google Keep","why":"quick notes"}],"why":"Google Sites creates clean web pages with embedded Docs, Sheets, and Slides.","tag":"03"},{"q":"In Google Docs, how do you export a finished document to PDF?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Edit → Paste without formatting</code>","why":"pastes plain text"},{"h":"<code>File → Download → PDF Document (.pdf)</code>","ok":1,"why":"exports a <code>.pdf</code> file"},{"h":"<code>Insert → Drawing</code>","why":"draws diagrams"},{"h":"<code>View → Mode → Viewing</code>","why":"switches view mode only"}],"why":"Use <code>File → Download → PDF Document (.pdf)</code>.","tag":"03"},{"q":"What happens if you turn on <strong>\"Make this a quiz\"</strong> in Google Forms Settings?","opts":[{"h":"Responses are deleted after 1 hour","why":"responses are kept"},{"h":"You can set an Answer Key, point values, and automatic grading for MCQs","ok":1,"why":"great for self-check quizzes"},{"h":"Only 5 people can submit","why":"no 5-person limit"},{"h":"It converts the form into Google Slides","why":"stays a Form"}],"why":"Quiz mode enables answer keys, point values, and auto-grading.","tag":"03"},{"q":"Which keyboard shortcut opens <strong>Find and Replace</strong> in Microsoft Word?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Ctrl+F</code>","why":"opens Find only"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+H</code>","ok":1,"why":"opens Find and Replace"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+J</code>","why":"Justify alignment"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+K</code>","why":"Insert Hyperlink"}],"why":"<code>Ctrl+H</code> opens Find &amp; Replace directly.","tag":"04"},{"q":"Which alignment stretches text evenly so both the left and right edges of a paragraph line up with the margins?","opts":[{"h":"Align Left (<code>Ctrl+L</code>)","why":"ragged right edge"},{"h":"Center (<code>Ctrl+E</code>)","why":"centered lines"},{"h":"Align Right (<code>Ctrl+R</code>)","why":"ragged left edge"},{"h":"Justify (<code>Ctrl+J</code>)","ok":1,"why":"aligns both left and right edges"}],"why":"Justify (<code>Ctrl+J</code>) is standard for formal reports and articles.","tag":"04"},{"q":"What does the <strong>Format Painter</strong> (<code>Home → Clipboard</code>) do in Word?","opts":[{"h":"Changes the page background color","why":"<code>Design → Page Color</code> does that"},{"h":"Copies font and paragraph formatting from selected text and applies it to other text","ok":1,"why":"saves re-applying bold/font/spacing manually"},{"h":"Checks grammar","why":"<code>Review → Editor</code> checks grammar"},{"h":"Inserts a picture","why":"<code>Insert → Pictures</code>"}],"why":"Format Painter copies formatting, not text content.","tag":"04"},{"q":"What does clicking the <strong><code>¶</code> (Show/Hide)</strong> button (<code>Home → Paragraph</code>) reveal?","opts":[{"h":"Page numbers","why":"shown in headers/footers"},{"h":"Hidden spaces, tab arrows, paragraph marks, and page/section breaks","ok":1,"why":"helps spot extra spaces or stray breaks"},{"h":"Word count","why":"shown in the status bar"},{"h":"Tracked comments","why":"shown in Review pane"}],"why":"<code>¶</code> reveals non-printing formatting symbols.","tag":"04"},{"q":"When pasting text from a website into Word without bringing weird background colors and fonts, which paste option should you use?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Ctrl+V</code> (Keep Source Formatting)","why":"keeps website styling"},{"h":"Paste Special → <strong>Keep Text Only</strong> (<code>Ctrl+Shift+V</code>)","ok":1,"why":"adopts your document's clean style"},{"h":"Screenshot paste","why":"pastes an uneditable image"},{"h":"Format Painter","why":"copies formatting after pasting"}],"why":"<strong>Keep Text Only</strong> strips unwanted web HTML styling.","tag":"04"},{"q":"Which shortcut <strong>Undoes</strong> your last action, and which <strong>Redoes</strong> it?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Ctrl+U</code> and <code>Ctrl+R</code>","why":"Underline and Right-align in Word"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+Z</code> (Undo) and <code>Ctrl+Y</code> (Redo)","ok":1,"why":"universal editing shortcuts"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+X</code> and <code>Ctrl+V</code>","why":"Cut and Paste"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+S</code> and <code>Ctrl+P</code>","why":"Save and Print"}],"why":"<code>Ctrl+Z</code> = Undo; <code>Ctrl+Y</code> = Redo.","tag":"04"},{"q":"Why is pressing <code>Enter</code> 15 times to push a new chapter onto the next page bad practice?","opts":[{"h":"Word crashes after 10 Enters","why":"Word doesn't crash"},{"h":"Any text added or deleted earlier shifts all those blank lines, misaligning the next page","ok":1,"why":"use <code>Ctrl+Enter</code> (Page Break) instead"},{"h":"It disables spellcheck","why":"unrelated"},{"h":"It turns the file into <code>.txt</code>","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"Use a <strong>Page Break</strong> (<code>Ctrl+Enter</code>) so chapters always start cleanly at the top of a page.","tag":"04"},{"q":"What must you apply to chapter titles so Word's <strong>Automatic Table of Contents</strong> (<code>References → Table of Contents</code>) detects them?","opts":[{"h":"Bold + 18 pt font manually","why":"TOC ignores manual font styling"},{"h":"Built-in Heading styles (<code>Home → Styles → Heading 1</code>, <code>Heading 2</code>, etc.)","ok":1,"why":"TOC reads Heading style levels"},{"h":"Highlight color","why":"ignored by TOC"},{"h":"Justify alignment","why":"ignored by TOC"}],"why":"Automatic TOC builds entries from <code>Heading 1</code>, <code>Heading 2</code>, <code>Heading 3</code> styles.","tag":"05"},{"q":"After editing your report and adding two pages, your Table of Contents page numbers are outdated. How do you fix them?","opts":[{"h":"Delete and retype every page number","why":"error-prone"},{"h":"Right-click the Table of Contents → <strong>Update Field → Update entire table</strong>","ok":1,"why":"refreshes headings and page numbers in one click"},{"h":"Export to <code>.txt</code>","why":"loses formatting"},{"h":"Press <code>Ctrl+H</code>","why":"Find &amp; Replace"}],"why":"Right-click TOC → <strong>Update Field</strong> refreshes all titles and page numbers.","tag":"05"},{"q":"Which break type is required if you want <strong>Page 4</strong> to be <strong>Landscape</strong> while the rest of the report remains <strong>Portrait</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"Line Break (<code>Shift+Enter</code>)","why":"breaks a line only"},{"h":"Page Break (<code>Ctrl+Enter</code>)","why":"shares the same page setup"},{"h":"<strong>Section Break (Next Page)</strong> (<code>Layout → Breaks → Next Page</code>)","ok":1,"why":"gives each section independent orientation and margins"},{"h":"Column Break","why":"moves to next column"}],"why":"Section Breaks isolate page orientation, margins, and headers/footers.","tag":"05"},{"q":"How do you hide the page number on <strong>Page 1</strong> (your cover page) while showing numbers <code>2, 3, 4...</code> on later pages?","opts":[{"h":"Delete the number on Page 1 manually","why":"deleting it removes it from ALL pages in that section!"},{"h":"Double-click the header/footer → tick <strong>Different First Page</strong> under Header &amp; Footer tools","ok":1,"why":"separates Page 1's header/footer from the rest"},{"h":"Change font color to white on Page 1","why":"still copies/selects in PDF"},{"h":"Turn off Track Changes","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"<strong>Different First Page</strong> gives Page 1 its own blank header/footer.","tag":"05"},{"q":"Which Ribbon tab holds <strong>Margins</strong>, <strong>Orientation</strong>, and <strong>Page Size</strong> in Microsoft Word?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Home</code>","why":"font, paragraph, styles"},{"h":"<code>Insert</code>","why":"tables, pictures, headers"},{"h":"<code>Layout</code> (or <code>Page Layout</code>)","ok":1,"why":"margins, orientation, size, columns, breaks"},{"h":"<code>Review</code>","why":"spelling, comments, Track Changes"}],"why":"Page setup options live on the <strong>Layout</strong> tab.","tag":"05"},{"q":"Which shortcut inserts a <strong>Page Break</strong> in Word?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Ctrl+B</code>","why":"Bold"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+Enter</code>","ok":1,"why":"Page Break"},{"h":"<code>Shift+Enter</code>","why":"Line Break (soft return)"},{"h":"<code>Alt+Enter</code>","why":"repeat / Excel newline"}],"why":"<code>Ctrl+Enter</code> inserts a Page Break.","tag":"05"},{"q":"What is the main advantage of using Word <strong>Styles</strong> (<code>Normal</code>, <code>Heading 1</code>, <code>Heading 2</code>) across a 30-page thesis?","opts":[{"h":"Word skips spellcheck on styled text","why":"spellcheck still runs"},{"h":"You can change the look of all headings at once by modifying the style, and auto-generate a Table of Contents","ok":1,"why":"keeps formatting consistent"},{"h":"It encrypts the <code>.docx</code>","why":"styles do not encrypt"},{"h":"It reduces page count by half","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"Styles ensure visual consistency and power the Navigation Pane and TOC.","tag":"05"},{"q":"Which Ribbon path adds an auto-numbered label like <code>Figure 1: System Diagram</code> below an image?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Home → Borders</code>","why":"adds borders"},{"h":"<code>References → Captions → Insert Caption</code> (or Right-click image → Insert Caption)","ok":1,"why":"automatically numbers figures and updates if reordered"},{"h":"<code>Layout → Position</code>","why":"positions image on page"},{"h":"<code>Review → New Comment</code>","why":"adds a review comment"}],"why":"<code>Insert Caption</code> auto-numbers figures and tables.","tag":"06"},{"q":"Where do you enable <strong>Track Changes</strong> in Microsoft Word?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Insert → Links</code>","why":"hyperlinks/bookmarks"},{"h":"<code>Design → Document Formatting</code>","why":"themes"},{"h":"<code>Review → Tracking → Track Changes</code> (<code>Ctrl+Shift+E</code>)","ok":1,"why":"records all edits for approval"},{"h":"<code>View → Show → Ruler</code>","why":"toggles ruler"}],"why":"Track Changes is under the <strong>Review</strong> tab (<code>Ctrl+Shift+E</code>).","tag":"06"},{"q":"Which Word feature keeps a table's column header row visible at the top of every new page when a long table spans multiple pages?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Home → Center</code>","why":"centers text"},{"h":"Table <strong>Layout</strong> tab → <strong>Repeat Header Rows</strong>","ok":1,"why":"automatically repeats the top header row on each page"},{"h":"<code>Insert → Page Number</code>","why":"numbers pages"},{"h":"<code>View → Split</code>","why":"splits editor window"}],"why":"Select the table's header row and enable <strong>Repeat Header Rows</strong>.","tag":"06"},{"q":"Which tab lets you choose a citation style (<strong>APA</strong>, <strong>IEEE</strong>, <strong>MLA</strong>) and insert a formatted <strong>Bibliography</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Home</code>","why":"clipboard, font, paragraph"},{"h":"<code>Layout</code>","why":"page setup"},{"h":"<code>References</code> (<code>References → Citations &amp; Bibliography</code>)","ok":1,"why":"manages sources and bibliographies"},{"h":"<code>Mailings</code>","why":"mail merge"}],"why":"Citations, Bibliography, Captions, and Table of Contents are all on the <strong>References</strong> tab.","tag":"06"},{"q":"What should you do with <strong>Track Changes</strong> before exporting your final report to PDF for submission?","opts":[{"h":"Leave all red deletions visible","why":"makes the final PDF look unfinished"},{"h":"<strong>Accept</strong> (or Reject) all changes and toggle <strong>Track Changes</strong> off","ok":1,"why":"produces a clean final document"},{"h":"Delete the Bibliography","why":"keep references"},{"h":"Convert tables to images","why":"keep real tables"}],"why":"Always resolve all tracked changes before final PDF export.","tag":"06"},{"q":"Which menu path exports a Word document to PDF?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Insert → Object</code>","why":"embeds objects"},{"h":"<code>File → Export → Create PDF/XPS</code> (or <code>File → Save As</code> → PDF)","ok":1,"why":"creates a <code>.pdf</code> file"},{"h":"<code>Review → Compare</code>","why":"compares two documents"},{"h":"<code>View → Print Layout</code>","why":"screen view mode"}],"why":"Use <code>File → Export → Create PDF/XPS</code> or <code>Save As → PDF</code>.","tag":"06"},{"q":"What character <strong>must</strong> every Excel formula begin with?","opts":[{"h":"<code>#</code>","why":"<code>#</code> starts error codes like <code>#DIV/0!</code>"},{"h":"<code>=</code>","ok":1,"why":"tells Excel to evaluate the cell as a formula"},{"h":"<code>@</code>","why":"used in mentions, not standard formula start"},{"h":"<code>$</code>","why":"<code>$</code> locks cell references inside a formula"}],"why":"Every Excel formula starts with <code>=</code>.","tag":"07"},{"q":"Cell <code>C2</code> has <code>=A2*B2</code>. You copy <code>C2</code> down one row to <code>C3</code>. What formula is in <code>C3</code>?","opts":[{"h":"<code>=A2*B2</code>","why":"relative references shift when copied"},{"h":"<code>=A3*B3</code>","ok":1,"why":"both relative row numbers increment by 1"},{"h":"<code>=B2*C2</code>","why":"copying down changes rows, not columns"},{"h":"<code>=$A$2*$B$2</code>","why":"no <code>$</code> locks were used"}],"why":"Relative references adjust automatically when dragged or copied.","tag":"07"},{"q":"You want every row in <code>D2:D20</code> to multiply its price (<code>C2</code>) by a single VAT rate stored in <code>F1</code>. Which formula in <code>D2</code> is correct before dragging down?","opts":[{"h":"<code>=C2*F1</code>","why":"<code>F1</code> will shift to <code>F2, F3...</code>"},{"h":"<code>=C2*$F$1</code>","ok":1,"why":"<code>$F$1</code> locks both column F and row 1"},{"h":"<code>=$C$2*F1</code>","why":"locks <code>C2</code> instead of <code>F1</code>"},{"h":"<code>=C2*&amp;F1</code>","why":"<code>&amp;</code> is invalid syntax here"}],"why":"Use <code>$F$1</code> (shortcut <code>F4</code>) to lock the single rate cell.","tag":"07"},{"q":"Which shortcut key cycles through <code>$A$1</code>, <code>A$1</code>, <code>$A1</code>, and <code>A1</code> while editing a cell reference in Excel's formula bar?","opts":[{"h":"<code>F1</code>","why":"Help"},{"h":"<code>F2</code>","why":"Edit active cell"},{"h":"<code>F4</code>","ok":1,"why":"cycles absolute/mixed <code>$</code> reference modes"},{"h":"<code>F5</code>","why":"Go To / Slide Show in PowerPoint"}],"why":"Pressing <code>F4</code> toggles <code>$</code> locks on the selected reference.","tag":"07"},{"q":"What does <code>###</code> inside an Excel cell indicate?","opts":[{"h":"Invalid formula syntax","why":"shows <code>#NAME?</code> or error dialog"},{"h":"The column is too narrow to display the formatted number or date","ok":1,"why":"double-click the column border to auto-fit"},{"h":"Division by zero","why":"shows <code>#DIV/0!</code>"},{"h":"Circular reference","why":"warns about self-referencing loop"}],"why":"Widen the column when Excel displays <code>###</code>.","tag":"07"},{"q":"Why should you type <code>150</code> and apply <strong>Currency</strong> formatting instead of typing <code>\"150 TL\"</code> manually into an Excel cell?","opts":[{"h":"<code>\"150 TL\"</code> deletes the cell","why":"it stays as text"},{"h":"Typing <code>\"TL\"</code> turns the cell into <strong>plain text</strong>, so <code>SUM</code> and math formulas ignore or fail on it","ok":1,"why":"number formatting displays <code>₺150</code> while keeping the value numeric <code>150</code>"},{"h":"Excel bans currency symbols","why":"Excel has built-in Currency/Accounting formats"},{"h":"It makes the font smaller","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"Keep numbers purely numeric and apply Number/Currency formatting for display.","tag":"07"},{"q":"What does the mixed reference <code>$A2</code> lock when copied across columns and down rows?","opts":[{"h":"Both column A and row 2","why":"that is <code>$A$2</code>"},{"h":"Only <strong>column A</strong> stays locked; row 2 can change","ok":1,"why":"<code>$</code> only locks the part immediately after it"},{"h":"Only <strong>row 2</strong> stays locked; column A can change","why":"that is <code>A$2</code>"},{"h":"Neither","why":"that is <code>A2</code>"}],"why":"<code>$</code> before <code>A</code> locks column <code>A</code>; without <code>$</code> before <code>2</code>, row <code>2</code> shifts when copied down.","tag":"07"},{"q":"Which is a valid Excel <strong>range</strong> representing a rectangle from column B row 2 to column D row 8?","opts":[{"h":"<code>B2-D8</code>","why":"hyphen is subtraction"},{"h":"<code>B2:D8</code>","ok":1,"why":"colon <code>:</code> defines a contiguous range"},{"h":"<code>B2;D8</code>","why":"semicolon separates function arguments in Turkish locale, not range endpoints"},{"h":"<code>B2..D8</code>","why":"not Excel syntax"}],"why":"Excel ranges use a colon: <code>StartCell:EndCell</code> (<code>B2:D8</code>).","tag":"07"},{"q":"Which Excel function returns the <strong>arithmetic mean</strong> of <code>B2:B10</code>?","opts":[{"h":"<code>=MEAN(B2:B10)</code>","why":"Excel uses <code>AVERAGE</code>, not <code>MEAN</code>"},{"h":"<code>=AVERAGE(B2:B10)</code>","ok":1,"why":"computes the average (<code>ORTALAMA</code> in Turkish)"},{"h":"<code>=SUM(B2:B10)</code>","why":"returns the total sum"},{"h":"<code>=COUNT(B2:B10)</code>","why":"counts numeric cells"}],"why":"Use <code>=AVERAGE(...)</code> (Turkish: <code>=ORTALAMA(...)</code>).","tag":"08"},{"q":"Cells <code>A1:A5</code> contain <code>10</code>, <code>\"Yes\"</code>, <em>(blank)</em>, <code>20</code>, and <code>\"No\"</code>. What does <code>=COUNT(A1:A5)</code> return?","opts":[{"h":"<code>2</code>","ok":1,"why":"<code>COUNT</code> counts <strong>numeric</strong> cells only (<code>10</code> and <code>20</code>)"},{"h":"<code>3</code>","why":"<code>3</code> is neither numeric count (<code>2</code>) nor non-empty (<code>4</code>)"},{"h":"<code>4</code>","why":"<code>4</code> is <code>=COUNTA(A1:A5)</code> (all non-empty cells)"},{"h":"<code>5</code>","why":"blank cell is not counted"}],"why":"<code>COUNT</code> counts numbers (<code>2</code>); <code>COUNTA</code> counts all non-empty cells (<code>4</code>).","tag":"08"},{"q":"What is the Turkish Excel equivalent of <code>=IF(B2&gt;=50, \"Pass\", \"Fail\")</code>?","opts":[{"h":"<code>=TOPLA(...)</code>","why":"<code>TOPLA</code> = <code>SUM</code>"},{"h":"<code>=ORTALAMA(...)</code>","why":"<code>ORTALAMA</code> = <code>AVERAGE</code>"},{"h":"<code>=EĞER(B2&gt;=50; \"Pass\"; \"Fail\")</code>","ok":1,"why":"<code>EĞER</code> = <code>IF</code> (with <code>;</code> separator in Turkish locale)"},{"h":"<code>=MAK(...)</code>","why":"<code>MAK</code> = <code>MAX</code>"}],"why":"Turkish Excel maps <code>SUM→TOPLA</code>, <code>AVERAGE→ORTALAMA</code>, <code>IF→EĞER</code>.","tag":"08"},{"q":"Which formula counts how many cells in <code>C2:C20</code> contain the word <code>\"Istanbul\"</code>?","opts":[{"h":"<code>=COUNT(C2:C20, \"Istanbul\")</code>","why":"<code>COUNT</code> does not accept criteria or count text"},{"h":"<code>=COUNTIF(C2:C20, \"Istanbul\")</code>","ok":1,"why":"counts cells in range matching <code>\"Istanbul\"</code>"},{"h":"<code>=IF(C2:C20=\"Istanbul\", 1, 0)</code>","why":"returns an array, not a single count"},{"h":"<code>=SUMIF(C2:C20, \"Istanbul\")</code>","why":"<code>SUMIF</code> sums numbers, not text"}],"why":"<code>COUNTIF(range, criteria)</code> counts cells matching a condition.","tag":"08"},{"q":"Which error does Excel show if a formula divides by <code>0</code> or an empty cell?","opts":[{"h":"<code>#NAME?</code>","why":"unknown function or unquoted text"},{"h":"<code>#DIV/0!</code>","ok":1,"why":"division by zero"},{"h":"<code>#VALUE!</code>","why":"incompatible data type (e.g., text + number)"},{"h":"<code>#REF!</code>","why":"deleted cell reference"}],"why":"Dividing by zero produces <code>#DIV/0!</code>.","tag":"08"},{"q":"Why does <code>=IF(B2&gt;=60, Pass, Fail)</code> produce a <strong><code>#NAME?</code></strong> error?","opts":[{"h":"<code>&gt;=</code> is invalid","why":"<code>&gt;=</code> is valid"},{"h":"Text strings <code>Pass</code> and <code>Fail</code> must be inside double quotes (<code>\"Pass\"</code>, <code>\"Fail\"</code>)","ok":1,"why":"without quotes, Excel looks for named ranges called <code>Pass</code> and <code>Fail</code>"},{"h":"<code>IF</code> needs 4 arguments","why":"<code>IF</code> takes 3 arguments"},{"h":"<code>B2</code> should be <code>$B$2</code>","why":"relative references are valid"}],"why":"Always wrap literal text in double quotes inside Excel formulas.","tag":"08"},{"q":"What does <code>=ROUND(3.14159, 2)</code> return?","opts":[{"h":"<code>3</code>","why":"<code>ROUND(..., 0)</code> returns <code>3</code>"},{"h":"<code>3.1</code>","why":"<code>ROUND(..., 1)</code> returns <code>3.1</code>"},{"h":"<code>3.14</code>","ok":1,"why":"rounds to 2 decimal places"},{"h":"<code>3.15</code>","why":"third digit is <code>1</code>, so it rounds down to <code>3.14</code>"}],"why":"<code>ROUND(number, 2)</code> rounds to 2 decimal places.","tag":"08"},{"q":"Which formula finds the <strong>smallest</strong> score in <code>D2:D30</code>?","opts":[{"h":"<code>=LOW(D2:D30)</code>","why":"not an Excel function"},{"h":"<code>=MIN(D2:D30)</code>","ok":1,"why":"returns minimum numeric value"},{"h":"<code>=MAX(D2:D30)</code>","why":"returns maximum"},{"h":"<code>=SMALL(D2:D30)</code>","why":"<code>SMALL</code> requires a second <code>k</code> argument"}],"why":"Use <code>=MIN(D2:D30)</code> for the smallest value and <code>=MAX(D2:D30)</code> for the largest.","tag":"08"},{"q":"Which shortcut toggles <strong>AutoFilter</strong> dropdown arrows on table headers in Excel?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Ctrl+F</code>","why":"Find"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+Shift+L</code>","ok":1,"why":"toggles Filter on/off (<code>Data → Filter</code>)"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+H</code>","why":"Replace"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+Enter</code>","why":"fills selection / Word page break"}],"why":"<code>Ctrl+Shift+L</code> toggles AutoFilter on the current table.","tag":"09"},{"q":"Which Excel feature automatically colors cells red when a student's grade is below <code>60</code>?","opts":[{"h":"Freeze Panes","why":"locks header rows while scrolling"},{"h":"Data Validation","why":"restricts what can be typed into a cell"},{"h":"<strong>Conditional Formatting</strong> (<code>Home → Conditional Formatting</code>)","ok":1,"why":"formats cells dynamically based on rules"},{"h":"Goal Seek","why":"solves for an input value"}],"why":"Conditional Formatting highlights cells matching value rules.","tag":"09"},{"q":"Which chart type is <strong>best</strong> for showing each browser's percentage share of a 100% total market?","opts":[{"h":"Line chart","why":"best for trends over time"},{"h":"Pie chart","ok":1,"why":"shows parts of a single whole (100%)"},{"h":"Scatter plot","why":"shows correlation between two variables"},{"h":"Stock chart","why":"shows financial high/low/close"}],"why":"Pie charts work best for a few slices summing to 100%.","tag":"09"},{"q":"Which chart type is <strong>best</strong> for comparing average scores across 6 different university departments?","opts":[{"h":"Column / Bar chart","ok":1,"why":"clearly compares discrete categories side by side"},{"h":"Pie chart","why":"hard to compare 6 close numeric averages visually"},{"h":"Area line chart","why":"implies continuous time trend"},{"h":"Bubble chart","why":"unnecessarily complex for 1 variable"}],"why":"Use Column or Bar charts to compare categories.","tag":"09"},{"q":"Which menu path keeps Row 1 visible while scrolling down through hundreds of rows?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Data → Sort</code>","why":"reorders rows"},{"h":"<code>View → Freeze Panes → Freeze Top Row</code>","ok":1,"why":"pins Row 1 at the top of the window"},{"h":"<code>Home → Merge &amp; Center</code>","why":"merges cells"},{"h":"<code>Page Layout → Print Titles</code>","why":"repeats headers on printed pages, not on screen"}],"why":"<code>View → Freeze Panes → Freeze Top Row</code> keeps Row 1 visible while scrolling.","tag":"09"},{"q":"What is the danger of highlighting <strong>only one column</strong> in a 4-column table and clicking Sort?","opts":[{"h":"Excel converts numbers to text","why":"unrelated"},{"h":"That column sorts independently of the other columns, scrambling which grade belongs to which student!","ok":1,"why":"click one cell inside the table or select all columns together"},{"h":"It deletes the header row","why":"headers stay or sort if unflagged"},{"h":"It turns off AutoSave","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"Always sort the entire table together so row records stay intact.","tag":"09"},{"q":"Where in PowerPoint do you add a logo or footer once so it automatically appears on <strong>every</strong> slide?","opts":[{"h":"On Slide 1 only","why":"appears only on Slide 1"},{"h":"<code>View → Slide Master</code> (on the top Master slide)","ok":1,"why":"global template controlling all layouts"},{"h":"<code>Slide Show → Rehearse Timings</code>","why":"practices timing"},{"h":"<code>Review → New Comment</code>","why":"adds review notes"}],"why":"Edit the top Slide Master to apply branding across all slides.","tag":"10"},{"q":"What is the modern standard <strong>Slide Size</strong> aspect ratio for classroom projectors and laptops?","opts":[{"h":"<code>4:3</code> Standard","why":"old square-ish projectors, leaves black bars on modern screens"},{"h":"<code>16:9</code> Widescreen (<code>Design → Slide Size</code>)","ok":1,"why":"matches modern HD/4K displays"},{"h":"<code>1:1</code> Square","why":"social media posts, not presentations"},{"h":"<code>9:16</code> Vertical","why":"phone stories, not projectors"}],"why":"Use <code>16:9</code> Widescreen (<code>Design → Slide Size → Widescreen</code>).","tag":"10"},{"q":"Why should you always click <strong>Close Master View</strong> after editing <code>View → Slide Master</code>?","opts":[{"h":"PowerPoint cannot save in Master View","why":"you can save, but you'll edit the template"},{"h":"So you don't accidentally type your actual slide content onto the template layouts","ok":1,"why":"Master View edits affect every slide using that layout"},{"h":"To delete all animations","why":"unrelated"},{"h":"To export to Excel","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"Exit Master View before authoring individual slides.","tag":"10"},{"q":"Where do you add <strong>Slide Numbers</strong> and hide them on the Title Slide?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Design → Format Background</code>","why":"background colors/images"},{"h":"<code>Insert → Header &amp; Footer</code> → tick <strong>Slide number</strong> and <strong>Don't show on title slide</strong> → <strong>Apply to All</strong>","ok":1,"why":"clean numbering"},{"h":"<code>Transitions → Timing</code>","why":"slide transition duration"},{"h":"<code>View → Outline View</code>","why":"text outline"}],"why":"Configure slide numbers and title-slide suppression in <code>Insert → Header &amp; Footer</code>.","tag":"10"},{"q":"Which tab lets you apply a coordinated color, font, and background style across an entire presentation?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Home</code>","why":"basic slide editing"},{"h":"<code>Design</code> (<code>Design → Themes</code>)","ok":1,"why":"sets overall theme and variants"},{"h":"<code>Animations</code>","why":"object motion"},{"h":"<code>Review</code>","why":"proofing and comments"}],"why":"Themes live under the <strong>Design</strong> tab.","tag":"10"},{"q":"What does the <strong>6×6 rule</strong> mean in slide design?","opts":[{"h":"Use 6 slides and 6 fonts","why":"use at most 2 fonts"},{"h":"Aim for at most ~6 bullet points per slide and ~6 words per bullet","ok":1,"why":"keeps slides readable and scannable"},{"h":"Use 6 pt font size","why":"6 pt is microscopic! Use ≥ 20 pt body text"},{"h":"Add 6 transitions per slide","why":"use 1 subtle transition"}],"why":"The 6×6 rule keeps bullets short so the audience listens to you instead of reading walls of text.","tag":"11"},{"q":"What is the minimum recommended <strong>body text size</strong> for classroom presentations?","opts":[{"h":"10 pt","why":"unreadable from the back row"},{"h":"12 pt","why":"good for Word reports, far too small for projectors"},{"h":"20–24 pt (at least 18–20 pt)","ok":1,"why":"clearly readable across a lecture hall"},{"h":"72 pt","why":"only for huge title slides"}],"why":"Keep slide body text at <strong>20 pt or larger</strong>.","tag":"11"},{"q":"Which PowerPoint feature converts a bulleted process list into a visual diagram (<code>Process</code>, <code>Cycle</code>, <code>Hierarchy</code>)?","opts":[{"h":"WordArt","why":"decorative text styles"},{"h":"<strong>SmartArt</strong> (<code>Home → Convert to SmartArt</code> or <code>Insert → SmartArt</code>)","ok":1,"why":"builds structured diagrams"},{"h":"Slide Sorter","why":"arranges slide thumbnails"},{"h":"Eyedropper","why":"picks colors"}],"why":"SmartArt turns text lists into clean visual diagrams.","tag":"11"},{"q":"When resizing a photo on a PowerPoint slide, which handle prevents stretching or squashing the image?","opts":[{"h":"Top edge handle","why":"distorts height"},{"h":"Side edge handle","why":"distorts width"},{"h":"Any <strong>corner</strong> handle","ok":1,"why":"scales width and height proportionally"},{"h":"Rotate handle","why":"rotates the image"}],"why":"Always drag a corner handle to preserve aspect ratio.","tag":"11"},{"q":"Which color combination gives the <strong>worst</strong> contrast on a bright classroom projector?","opts":[{"h":"Black text on white background","why":"high contrast"},{"h":"White text on deep navy background","why":"high contrast"},{"h":"Light yellow text on a white background","ok":1,"why":"nearly invisible from a distance"},{"h":"Dark navy text on cream background","why":"good contrast"}],"why":"Avoid light-on-light or dark-on-dark color pairings.","tag":"11"},{"q":"What is the key difference between <strong>Transitions</strong> and <strong>Animations</strong> in PowerPoint?","opts":[{"h":"Transitions only work on text","why":"Transitions apply to whole slides"},{"h":"<strong>Transitions</strong> control how one <strong>slide</strong> moves to the next; <strong>Animations</strong> control how individual <strong>objects</strong> on a slide appear or move","ok":1,"why":"separate Ribbon tabs"},{"h":"Animations cannot be timed","why":"Animation Pane controls exact timing"},{"h":"Transitions require video files","why":"built-in effects"}],"why":"Transitions = between slides; Animations = objects on a slide.","tag":"12"},{"q":"Which PowerPoint sidebar lets you reorder object animations and change triggers (<code>On Click</code>, <code>With Previous</code>, <code>After Previous</code>)?","opts":[{"h":"Selection Pane","why":"hides/renames objects"},{"h":"<strong>Animation Pane</strong> (<code>Animations → Animation Pane</code>)","ok":1,"why":"shows animation timeline and order"},{"h":"Notes Pane","why":"speaker notes"},{"h":"Format Pane","why":"shape/fill properties"}],"why":"Use the <strong>Animation Pane</strong> to control animation order and timing.","tag":"12"},{"q":"Which keyboard shortcut starts Slide Show from <strong>Slide 1</strong>, and which starts from the <strong>current slide</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"<code>F1</code> and <code>Shift+F1</code>","why":"Help"},{"h":"<code>F5</code> (from Slide 1) and <code>Shift+F5</code> (from current slide)","ok":1,"why":"standard presenter shortcuts"},{"h":"<code>F4</code> and <code>Shift+F4</code>","why":"Repeat / Find Next"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+P</code> and <code>Ctrl+S</code>","why":"Pen / Save"}],"why":"<code>F5</code> = From Beginning; <code>Shift+F5</code> = From Current Slide.","tag":"12"},{"q":"What does <strong>Presenter View</strong> show on your laptop screen while the projector shows only the clean slide?","opts":[{"h":"Only a black screen","why":"<code>B</code> turns the projector black"},{"h":"Your <strong>Speaker Notes</strong>, a <strong>timer</strong>, and a preview of the <strong>next slide</strong>","ok":1,"why":"keeps notes private from the audience"},{"h":"The Slide Master editor","why":"editor is hidden during Slide Show"},{"h":"Your desktop wallpaper","why":"shows Presenter View"}],"why":"Presenter View gives you notes, timing, and next-slide preview privately.","tag":"12"},{"q":"Why is <strong>embedding</strong> a local MP4 video (<code>Insert → Video → This Device</code>) safer than linking to an online YouTube URL for a classroom talk?","opts":[{"h":"Embedded videos have lower quality","why":"embedded MP4 keeps full quality"},{"h":"Classroom Wi-Fi or internet firewalls may fail during your talk, whereas an embedded video plays offline inside the <code>.pptx</code>","ok":1,"why":"always test media offline"},{"h":"YouTube videos cannot play in <code>16:9</code>","why":"unrelated"},{"h":"Embedded videos are automatically converted to PDF","why":"PDFs don't play MP4s"}],"why":"Embedding local media ensures offline reliability during presentations.","tag":"12"},{"q":"During a live Slide Show, pressing <strong><code>B</code></strong> on the keyboard:","opts":[{"h":"Ends the presentation","why":"<code>Esc</code> ends it"},{"h":"Turns the projector screen <strong>black</strong> so the audience focuses on you","ok":1,"why":"press <code>B</code> again to resume"},{"h":"Switches to Bold text","why":"<code>Ctrl+B</code> in edit mode"},{"h":"Saves a backup","why":"<code>Ctrl+S</code> saves"}],"why":"<code>B</code> = Black screen, <code>W</code> = White screen during Slide Show.","tag":"13"},{"q":"Which shortcut activates the <strong>Pen</strong> tool during a live PowerPoint Slide Show so you can circle items on screen?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Ctrl+B</code>","why":"Bold in edit mode"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+P</code>","ok":1,"why":"activates live Pen (<code>E</code> erases drawings)"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+H</code>","why":"hides cursor / Find &amp; Replace in edit"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+Z</code>","why":"Undo"}],"why":"<code>Ctrl+P</code> turns the cursor into a drawing pen during Slide Show.","tag":"13"},{"q":"You used a custom downloaded font in <code>.pptx</code> and will present on a different computer. What are the two safest precautions?","opts":[{"h":"Delete all slide numbers and animations","why":"does not fix missing fonts"},{"h":"Turn on <strong>Embed fonts in the file</strong> (<code>File → Options → Save</code>) AND bring an exported <strong>PDF</strong> backup (<code>File → Export → Create PDF/XPS</code>)","ok":1,"why":"guarantees layout never shifts"},{"h":"Save as <code>.csv</code>","why":"CSV is for tables"},{"h":"Rename <code>.pptx</code> to <code>.pdf</code>","why":"corrupts the file"}],"why":"Embed fonts in <code>.pptx</code> and always carry a PDF backup.","tag":"13"},{"q":"Which Print layout prints <strong>3 slide thumbnails per page</strong> with ruled lines beside them for audience notes?","opts":[{"h":"Full Page Slides","why":"1 slide per page"},{"h":"<code>6 Slides Horizontal</code>","why":"6 slides, no note lines"},{"h":"<code>3 Slides</code> (Handouts)","ok":1,"why":"includes blank note-taking lines next to each slide"},{"h":"Outline View","why":"text only"}],"why":"Choose <code>File → Print → Handouts → 3 Slides</code> for note-taking handouts.","tag":"13"},{"q":"Which search query finds PowerPoint decks (<code>.pptx</code>) about <code>cloud computing</code>?","opts":[{"h":"<code>cloud computing pptx</code>","why":"finds web pages mentioning the word pptx"},{"h":"<code>\"cloud computing\" filetype:pptx</code>","ok":1,"why":"filters for exact phrase and <code>.pptx</code> files"},{"h":"<code>site:pptx \"cloud computing\"</code>","why":"<code>site:</code> expects a domain"},{"h":"<code>cloud computing -pptx</code>","why":"excludes <code>.pptx</code>"}],"why":"Use <code>filetype:pptx</code> to search specifically for PowerPoint files.","tag":"01"},{"q":"Why should you avoid using <code>\"Re: Hi\"</code> or leaving the subject blank on an email to a lecturer?","opts":[{"h":"Email servers reject blank subjects","why":"servers deliver them, but humans ignore or filter them"},{"h":"It looks unprofessional and makes it hard for the lecturer to know which course or request you are writing about","ok":1,"why":"include course code and topic"},{"h":"It disables attachments","why":"attachments still work"},{"h":"It sends the email via BCC","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"A clear subject line helps recipients prioritize and find your message.","tag":"01"},{"q":"Which e-commerce model describes an online bookstore like Amazon Retail selling books directly to shoppers?","opts":[{"h":"B2B","why":"business to business"},{"h":"B2C","ok":1,"why":"Business-to-Consumer"},{"h":"C2C","why":"consumer to consumer"},{"h":"C2B","why":"consumer to business"}],"why":"Retail stores selling to individual consumers are B2C.","tag":"01"},{"q":"Which file format is best for importing a clean table of 500 students into Excel or SQLite without extra formatting?","opts":[{"h":"<code>.docx</code>","why":"Word document"},{"h":"<code>.pdf</code>","why":"fixed layout"},{"h":"<code>.csv</code>","ok":1,"why":"plain-text comma-separated table"},{"h":"<code>.pptx</code>","why":"presentation slides"}],"why":"<code>.csv</code> is the universal plain-text tabular exchange format.","tag":"02"},{"q":"What happens when you compress a 10 MB folder into a <code>.zip</code> file?","opts":[{"h":"All files inside are permanently deleted","why":"originals remain untouched"},{"h":"The folder is bundled into one smaller archive file that can be extracted later","ok":1,"why":"ideal for email and portal uploads"},{"h":"Every <code>.docx</code> turns into <code>.pdf</code>","why":"formats inside stay the same"},{"h":"It becomes read-only forever","why":"files can be unzipped and edited"}],"why":"<code>.zip</code> archives bundle and compress files/folders without losing data.","tag":"02"},{"q":"Which Windows File Explorer setting lets you see <code>.docx</code>, <code>.pdf</code>, and <code>.exe</code> at the end of filenames?","opts":[{"h":"<code>View → Large icons</code>","why":"changes icon size"},{"h":"<code>View → Show → File name extensions</code> (or <code>View → File name extensions</code>)","ok":1,"why":"reveals true extensions"},{"h":"<code>Home → Pin to Quick access</code>","why":"pins folder"},{"h":"<code>Share → Zip</code>","why":"creates archive"}],"why":"Enabling File name extensions prevents mistaking file types.","tag":"02"},{"q":"In Google Docs, how do you mention a teammate so they get an email notification about a comment?","opts":[{"h":"Type <code>#name</code>","why":"hashtags don't notify in Docs"},{"h":"Insert a Comment (<code>Ctrl+Alt+M</code>) and type <code>@</code> followed by their email/name","ok":1,"why":"assigns/notifies the teammate"},{"h":"Bold their name","why":"no notification"},{"h":"Change font to red","why":"no notification"}],"why":"Typing <code>@email</code> inside a Google Docs comment notifies and optionally assigns the action item.","tag":"03"},{"q":"In Google Forms, which question type allows respondents to pick <strong>more than one</strong> option (e.g., \"Select all languages you know\")?","opts":[{"h":"Multiple choice","why":"allows only 1 choice"},{"h":"Checkboxes","ok":1,"why":"allows selecting multiple options"},{"h":"Linear scale","why":"picks 1 number on a scale"},{"h":"Short answer","why":"free text"}],"why":"Use <strong>Checkboxes</strong> for multi-select questions and <strong>Multiple choice</strong> for single-select.","tag":"03"},{"q":"Where do you publish a <strong>Google Site</strong> so visitors can view it with a link?","opts":[{"h":"<code>File → Print</code>","why":"prints pages"},{"h":"Click the <strong>Publish</strong> button in the top-right corner","ok":1,"why":"sets web address and visibility"},{"h":"<code>Responses → Link to Sheets</code>","why":"Google Forms feature"},{"h":"<code>Slide Show → F5</code>","why":"PowerPoint shortcut"}],"why":"Click <strong>Publish</strong> in Google Sites to make your site live.","tag":"03"},{"q":"Which keyboard shortcut applies <strong>Italic</strong> formatting in Word, Excel, and PowerPoint?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Ctrl+B</code>","why":"Bold"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+I</code>","ok":1,"why":"Italic"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+U</code>","why":"Underline"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+J</code>","why":"Justify (Word)"}],"why":"<code>Ctrl+B</code> = Bold, <code>Ctrl+I</code> = Italic, <code>Ctrl+U</code> = Underline.","tag":"04"},{"q":"Which shortcut <strong>Selects All</strong> content in the current document or slide?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Ctrl+A</code>","ok":1,"why":"Select All"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+S</code>","why":"Save"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+C</code>","why":"Copy"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+X</code>","why":"Cut"}],"why":"<code>Ctrl+A</code> selects all text/items.","tag":"04"},{"q":"You want to replace every occurrence of <code>\"IGU\"</code> with <code>\"İGÜ\"</code> across a 15-page Word file. Which shortcut opens the tool?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Ctrl+F</code>","why":"Find only"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+H</code>","ok":1,"why":"Find and Replace (click <strong>Replace All</strong>)"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+Z</code>","why":"Undo"},{"h":"<code>Ctrl+P</code>","why":"Print"}],"why":"Press <code>Ctrl+H</code> and use Replace All.","tag":"04"},{"q":"In Word, which view on the left sidebar lets you jump quickly between <code>Heading 1</code> and <code>Heading 2</code> chapters?","opts":[{"h":"Print Preview","why":"shows printed pages"},{"h":"<strong>Navigation Pane</strong> (<code>View → Show → Navigation Pane</code> or <code>Ctrl+F</code> → Headings tab)","ok":1,"why":"displays document heading outline"},{"h":"Macro Viewer","why":"VBA macros"},{"h":"Ruler","why":"sets margins and tabs"}],"why":"Heading styles populate both the Table of Contents and the Navigation Pane.","tag":"05"},{"q":"Where do you change page margins (e.g., Narrow vs. Normal) in Microsoft Word?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Home → Font</code>","why":"font settings"},{"h":"<code>Insert → Pages</code>","why":"cover/blank/page break"},{"h":"<code>Layout → Page Setup → Margins</code>","ok":1,"why":"controls top, bottom, left, right margins"},{"h":"<code>References → Footnotes</code>","why":"footnotes"}],"why":"Margins, Orientation, and Size live under <code>Layout → Page Setup</code>.","tag":"05"},{"q":"What is the difference between <code>Shift+Enter</code> and <code>Ctrl+Enter</code> in Word?","opts":[{"h":"Both insert a new page","why":"<code>Shift+Enter</code> stays on the same page"},{"h":"<code>Shift+Enter</code> starts a new line inside the <strong>same paragraph</strong>; <code>Ctrl+Enter</code> starts a <strong>new page</strong>","ok":1,"why":"useful inside bullet lists vs. chapters"},{"h":"Both insert a Section Break","why":"Section Breaks are in <code>Layout → Breaks</code>"},{"h":"<code>Shift+Enter</code> deletes the line","why":"never"}],"why":"<code>Shift+Enter</code> = soft line break; <code>Ctrl+Enter</code> = Page Break.","tag":"05"},{"q":"In Microsoft Word, which tab contains <strong>Spelling &amp; Grammar (Editor)</strong>, <strong>Word Count</strong>, and <strong>Track Changes</strong>?","opts":[{"h":"<code>References</code>","why":"TOC, captions, citations"},{"h":"<code>Review</code>","ok":1,"why":"proofing, comments, tracking, compare"},{"h":"<code>Mailings</code>","why":"envelopes, mail merge"},{"h":"<code>Design</code>","why":"themes, colors, watermark"}],"why":"Proofing and collaboration tools live on the <strong>Review</strong> tab.","tag":"06"},{"q":"After inserting a new figure above <code>Figure 1</code>, how do you update caption numbers if one didn't refresh immediately?","opts":[{"h":"Retype every figure number","why":"error-prone"},{"h":"Select all (<code>Ctrl+A</code>) and press <strong><code>F9</code></strong> (Update Fields)","ok":1,"why":"refreshes all captions, cross-references, and TOC fields"},{"h":"Save as <code>.txt</code>","why":"loses formatting"},{"h":"Restart Windows","why":"unnecessary"}],"why":"Pressing <code>F9</code> updates Word fields including captions and TOC.","tag":"06"},{"q":"What is a <strong>cross-reference</strong> (<code>References → Captions → Cross-reference</code>) used for in Word?","opts":[{"h":"Deleting duplicate words","why":"Find &amp; Replace"},{"h":"Inserting a clickable link in text like <code>\"see Figure 2\"</code> that updates automatically if the figure number changes","ok":1,"why":"keeps text references accurate"},{"h":"Drawing arrows on images","why":"<code>Insert → Shapes</code>"},{"h":"Merging two tables","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"Cross-references keep in-text mentions (<code>Figure 2</code>, <code>Table 1</code>) synchronized automatically.","tag":"06"},{"q":"Which Excel error appears when you delete a row or column that a formula was pointing to?","opts":[{"h":"<code>#DIV/0!</code>","why":"division by zero"},{"h":"<code>#NAME?</code>","why":"unknown function or unquoted name"},{"h":"<code>#REF!</code>","ok":1,"why":"invalid/deleted cell reference"},{"h":"<code>###</code>","why":"narrow column"}],"why":"<code>#REF!</code> means a referenced cell no longer exists.","tag":"07"},{"q":"What does <code>F2</code> do when a cell is selected in Excel?","opts":[{"h":"Saves the workbook","why":"<code>Ctrl+S</code>"},{"h":"Enters <strong>Edit mode</strong> inside the selected cell (and highlights referenced cells in color)","ok":1,"why":"quick keyboard editing"},{"h":"Locks <code>$A$1</code>","why":"<code>F4</code> locks <code>$</code>"},{"h":"Opens Filter","why":"<code>Ctrl+Shift+L</code>"}],"why":"Press <code>F2</code> to edit a cell's contents/formula directly.","tag":"07"},{"q":"When dragging <code>=A$1*B2</code> <strong>down</strong> from Row 2 to Row 3, what does the formula become?","opts":[{"h":"<code>=A$1*B2</code>","why":"<code>B2</code> is relative so it shifts"},{"h":"<code>=A$1*B3</code>","ok":1,"why":"<code>$1</code> locks row 1, while <code>B2</code> shifts to <code>B3</code>"},{"h":"<code>=A$2*B3</code>","why":"<code>$1</code> stays locked at row 1"},{"h":"<code>=$A$1*B3</code>","why":"<code>A</code> had no <code>$</code>, though dragging down doesn't change column <code>A</code> anyway"}],"why":"Mixed reference <code>A$1</code> locks row 1 when copied vertically.","tag":"07"},{"q":"Which Excel function returns <strong>how many non-empty cells</strong> (both text and numbers) are in <code>A1:A10</code>?","opts":[{"h":"<code>COUNT(A1:A10)</code>","why":"counts numbers only"},{"h":"<code>COUNTA(A1:A10)</code>","ok":1,"why":"counts all non-blank cells"},{"h":"<code>SUM(A1:A10)</code>","why":"sums numbers"},{"h":"<code>LEN(A1:A10)</code>","why":"returns character length of one string"}],"why":"<code>COUNTA</code> counts every cell that is not empty.","tag":"08"},{"q":"What does <code>=MAX(12, 45, 7, 30)</code> return?","opts":[{"h":"<code>7</code>","why":"<code>MIN</code> returns <code>7</code>"},{"h":"<code>23.5</code>","why":"<code>AVERAGE</code> returns <code>23.5</code>"},{"h":"<code>45</code>","ok":1,"why":"largest value in the list"},{"h":"<code>94</code>","why":"<code>SUM</code> returns <code>94</code>"}],"why":"<code>MAX</code> returns the highest numeric value (<code>45</code>).","tag":"08"},{"q":"What is the Turkish Excel name for <code>SUM</code>?","opts":[{"h":"<code>ORTALAMA</code>","why":"<code>AVERAGE</code>"},{"h":"<code>TOPLA</code>","ok":1,"why":"<code>SUM</code>"},{"h":"<code>EĞER</code>","why":"<code>IF</code>"},{"h":"<code>MAK</code>","why":"<code>MAX</code>"}],"why":"<code>SUM</code> in Turkish Excel is <code>TOPLA</code>.","tag":"08"},{"q":"Which formula returns <code>1</code> if <code>A1</code> is <code>\"Yes\"</code> and <code>0</code> otherwise?","opts":[{"h":"<code>=IF(A1=\"Yes\", 1, 0)</code>","ok":1,"why":"checks <code>A1=\"Yes\"</code>, returns <code>1</code> or <code>0</code>"},{"h":"<code>=IF(A1=Yes, 1, 0)</code>","why":"<code>Yes</code> without quotes causes <code>#NAME?</code>"},{"h":"<code>=COUNT(A1=\"Yes\")</code>","why":"invalid use of <code>COUNT</code>"},{"h":"<code>=SUMIF(A1, \"Yes\", 1)</code>","why":"<code>SUMIF</code> expects a range for sum_range"}],"why":"Quote <code>\"Yes\"</code> and use <code>=IF(A1=\"Yes\", 1, 0)</code>.","tag":"08"},{"q":"Which Excel feature lets you keep <strong>both</strong> Row 1 and Column A visible while scrolling right and down?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Freeze Top Row</code>","why":"freezes only Row 1"},{"h":"<code>Freeze First Column</code>","why":"freezes only Column A"},{"h":"Select cell <strong><code>B2</code></strong>, then click <code>View → Freeze Panes → Freeze Panes</code>","ok":1,"why":"freezes everything above (<code>Row 1</code>) and left (<code>Col A</code>) of <code>B2</code>"},{"h":"<code>Split Window</code>","why":"creates separate scrollable panes rather than pinned headers"}],"why":"Selecting <code>B2</code> and clicking <code>Freeze Panes</code> locks both Row 1 and Column A.","tag":"09"},{"q":"Which chart is <strong>least suitable</strong> for a table with 18 small categories?","opts":[{"h":"Pie chart","ok":1,"why":"18 tiny slices are impossible to read or compare"},{"h":"Horizontal Bar chart","why":"easy to read 18 labels cleanly"},{"h":"Column chart","why":"readable with angled/clean labels"},{"h":"Sorted Bar chart","why":"best for many categories"}],"why":"Avoid Pie charts when there are more than ~5–6 categories.","tag":"09"},{"q":"Where in Excel do you set <strong>Landscape</strong> orientation and <strong>Fit Sheet on One Page</strong> before printing?","opts":[{"h":"<code>Insert → Charts</code>","why":"charts"},{"h":"<code>Page Layout → Page Setup / Scale to Fit</code> (or <code>File → Print</code>)","ok":1,"why":"controls print orientation and scaling"},{"h":"<code>Data → Filter</code>","why":"filtering"},{"h":"<code>Review → Protect Sheet</code>","why":"sheet protection"}],"why":"<code>Page Layout</code> controls print orientation, margins, and scaling.","tag":"09"},{"q":"In PowerPoint, what is a <strong>Placeholder</strong> on a Slide Layout?","opts":[{"h":"A permanent locked image","why":"placeholders hold editable content"},{"h":"A dotted-border container (for Title, Text, Chart, Picture) defined by the Layout","ok":1,"why":"keeps alignment consistent across slides"},{"h":"A slide transition","why":"transitions are between slides"},{"h":"A speaker note","why":"notes sit below the slide"}],"why":"Using layout placeholders keeps text positions and Outline View clean.","tag":"10"},{"q":"Which view in PowerPoint shows small thumbnails of <strong>all</strong> slides in a grid so you can easily drag to reorder or delete slides?","opts":[{"h":"Normal View","why":"edits one slide at a time"},{"h":"<strong>Slide Sorter</strong> (<code>View → Slide Sorter</code>)","ok":1,"why":"grid of all slide thumbnails"},{"h":"Notes Page","why":"shows 1 slide + speaker notes"},{"h":"Reading View","why":"previews presentation in a window"}],"why":"Slide Sorter is ideal for reordering slides and checking visual flow.","tag":"10"},{"q":"Why is a dark photo background with thin white text risky on a classroom projector?","opts":[{"h":"Projectors cannot show photos","why":"they can, just with lower contrast"},{"h":"Bright areas of the photo wash out the white text, hurting readability","ok":1,"why":"add a semi-transparent dark overlay box or use a solid background"},{"h":"It makes the <code>.pptx</code> impossible to save","why":"saves fine"},{"h":"It disables animations","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"Always ensure high contrast behind every word on a slide.","tag":"11"},{"q":"How can you link an <strong>Excel chart</strong> into PowerPoint so updating numbers in Excel can update the slide chart?","opts":[{"h":"Take a screenshot with <code>Win+Shift+S</code>","why":"static image, never updates"},{"h":"Copy the chart in Excel and paste in PowerPoint using <strong>Keep Source Formatting &amp; Link Data</strong>","ok":1,"why":"links back to the <code>.xlsx</code> file"},{"h":"Export the Excel sheet to <code>.txt</code>","why":"loses chart"},{"h":"Type the numbers into a SmartArt graphic","why":"not linked to Excel"}],"why":"Linking Excel data keeps slide charts synchronized with spreadsheet updates.","tag":"11"},{"q":"Which PowerPoint animation category makes an object <strong>appear onto</strong> the slide (such as <code>Fade</code> or <code>Fly In</code>)?","opts":[{"h":"<strong>Entrance</strong> (green icons)","ok":1,"why":"brings objects onto the slide"},{"h":"<strong>Emphasis</strong> (yellow icons)","why":"highlights an object already on the slide"},{"h":"<strong>Exit</strong> (red icons)","why":"removes an object from the slide"},{"h":"<strong>Motion Paths</strong>","why":"moves an object along a path"}],"why":"Green = Entrance, Yellow = Emphasis, Red = Exit.","tag":"12"},{"q":"Why should you set bullet animations to <strong>On Click</strong> (By Paragraph) rather than showing all 6 bullets immediately?","opts":[{"h":"It reduces file size","why":"same size"},{"h":"It prevents the audience from reading Bullet #5 while you are still explaining Bullet #1","ok":1,"why":"keeps attention synchronized with your voice"},{"h":"PowerPoint requires it to save","why":"optional"},{"h":"It turns on Presenter View","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"Revealing bullets one by one keeps the audience focused on your current point.","tag":"12"},{"q":"During a live PowerPoint presentation, which key exits Slide Show mode and returns to the editor?","opts":[{"h":"<code>B</code>","why":"Black screen"},{"h":"<code>W</code>","why":"White screen"},{"h":"<code>Esc</code>","ok":1,"why":"exits Slide Show"},{"h":"<code>F5</code>","why":"restarts Slide Show from Slide 1"}],"why":"Press <code>Esc</code> to end Slide Show.","tag":"13"},{"q":"Which export option turns a timed or narrated PowerPoint presentation into a standalone <code>.mp4</code> movie?","opts":[{"h":"<code>File → Export → Create PDF/XPS</code>","why":"static pages"},{"h":"<code>File → Export → Create a Video</code>","ok":1,"why":"renders slides, timings, and audio to <code>.mp4</code>"},{"h":"<code>File → Save As → .csv</code>","why":"invalid for presentations"},{"h":"<code>Slide Show → Rehearse Timings</code>","why":"records timings before exporting"}],"why":"<code>File → Export → Create a Video</code> produces a playable video file.","tag":"13"},{"q":"What does <code>File → Print → Full Page Slides</code> → <strong><code>6 Slides Horizontal</code></strong> do?","opts":[{"h":"Deletes 6 slides","why":"prints only"},{"h":"Prints 6 slide thumbnails per page as a compact handout","ok":1,"why":"saves paper for study handouts"},{"h":"Runs Slide Show 6 times","why":"printing only"},{"h":"Exports 6 PDFs","why":"prints/exports one document"}],"why":"<code>6 Slides Horizontal</code> creates compact multi-slide handouts.","tag":"13"},{"q":"What is the difference between the Internet and the World Wide Web?","opts":[{"h":"They are the same thing","why":"the Web is only one service on the Internet"},{"h":"The Internet is the global network; the Web is a service of linked pages that runs on it","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"The Web is older than the Internet","why":"the Internet came first (ARPANET 1969, Web 1989–91)"},{"h":"The Internet is only for email","why":"email is one service on it"},{"h":"The Web works without the Internet","why":"the Web needs the Internet"}],"why":"Internet = network; Web = pages + links + browsers.","tag":"01"},{"q":"A padlock icon and \"https://\" in the address bar mean that:","opts":[{"h":"the site is government-approved","why":"no"},{"h":"the connection between your browser and the site is encrypted","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"the site has no cookies","why":"unrelated"},{"h":"the site is free","why":"unrelated"},{"h":"the page is saved offline","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"HTTPS = encrypted HTTP.","tag":"01"},{"q":"An email from \"Gelisim-Support &lt;help@gelisim-verify.net&gt;\" asks you to confirm your password with a link. This is most likely:","opts":[{"h":"spam advertising","why":"it asks for credentials, which is more dangerous"},{"h":"phishing","ok":1,"why":"a fake sender trying to steal your login"},{"h":"a malicious attachment","why":"there is no attachment"},{"h":"a BCC message","why":"BCC is an email field"},{"h":"a cookie","why":"not related"}],"why":"Check the real sender domain; universities never ask for passwords by email.","tag":"01"},{"q":"Which e-commerce model is a company selling laptops to a ministry through a tender?","opts":[{"h":"B2C","why":"consumer"},{"h":"C2C","why":"consumers"},{"h":"B2G","ok":1,"why":"business to government"},{"h":"C2B","why":"consumer to business"},{"h":"B2B","why":"the buyer is a government, not a business"}],"why":"B2G = business to government.","tag":"01"},{"q":"Which browser feature does NOT keep history or cookies after you close the window?","opts":[{"h":"Bookmarks","why":"saves links"},{"h":"Cache","why":"stores files"},{"h":"Private / Incognito window","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"Home page","why":"startup page"},{"h":"Downloads","why":"a list of files"}],"why":"Incognito: <code>Ctrl+Shift+N</code> in Chrome.","tag":"01"},{"q":"You send a newsletter to 200 students and do not want them to see each other's addresses. Put the addresses in:","opts":[{"h":"To","why":"everyone sees them"},{"h":"CC","why":"everyone sees them"},{"h":"BCC","ok":1,"why":"hidden from other receivers"},{"h":"Subject","why":"no"},{"h":"Signature","why":"no"}],"why":"BCC = blind carbon copy.","tag":"01"},{"q":"Which Google Forms question type lets respondents choose MORE than one option?","opts":[{"h":"Multiple choice","why":"only one option"},{"h":"Checkboxes","ok":1,"why":"one or more options"},{"h":"Dropdown","why":"only one option"},{"h":"Linear scale","why":"one number"},{"h":"Short answer","why":"free text"}],"why":"Checkboxes = several; multiple choice = one.","tag":"03"},{"q":"Which Google Forms question type requires respondents to sign in to a Google account?","opts":[{"h":"Paragraph","why":"no sign-in needed"},{"h":"Date","why":"no sign-in needed"},{"h":"File upload","ok":1,"why":"files are stored in the form owner's Drive"},{"h":"Linear scale","why":"no sign-in needed"},{"h":"Checkbox grid","why":"no sign-in needed"}],"why":"File upload needs sign-in.","tag":"03"},{"q":"In Google Calendar, how do you add a video meeting link to an event?","opts":[{"h":"Insert → Video","why":"not a Calendar menu"},{"h":"Click \"Add Google Meet video conferencing\" in the event","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"Email the guests a phone number","why":"not a Meet link"},{"h":"Share the calendar publicly","why":"no"},{"h":"Use Version history","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"The Meet link is created automatically.","tag":"03"},{"q":"A Google Drive user who can add comments but cannot change the text has the role:","opts":[{"h":"Viewer","why":"cannot comment"},{"h":"Commenter","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"Editor","why":"can change text"},{"h":"Owner","why":"full control"},{"h":"Guest","why":"not a Drive role"}],"why":"Viewer &lt; Commenter &lt; Editor.","tag":"03"},{"q":"Where can you restore an older version of a Google Doc?","opts":[{"h":"Edit → Undo","why":"only recent actions"},{"h":"File → Version history","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"Insert → Bookmark","why":"unrelated"},{"h":"Tools → Spelling","why":"unrelated"},{"h":"Share → General access","why":"permissions"}],"why":"Version history keeps earlier versions.","tag":"03"},{"q":"Which Word view opens when you click the File tab?","opts":[{"h":"Print Layout","why":"a document view"},{"h":"Backstage view","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"Outline view","why":"a document view"},{"h":"Read Mode","why":"a document view"},{"h":"Draft view","why":"a document view"}],"why":"File tab = Backstage view.","tag":"04"},{"q":"Which file extension is a Word template?","opts":[{"h":".docx","why":"normal document"},{"h":".docm","why":"document with macros"},{"h":".dotx","ok":1,"why":"template"},{"h":".pdf","why":"fixed-layout file"},{"h":".xlsx","why":"Excel workbook"}],"why":".dotx = Word template.","tag":"04"},{"q":"Before emailing a report, you want to remove hidden comments and the author name. Use:","opts":[{"h":"Protect Document → Mark as Final","why":"doesn't remove data"},{"h":"File → Info → Check for Issues → Inspect Document","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"Review → Spelling &amp; Grammar","why":"unrelated"},{"h":"Home → Clear All Formatting","why":"removes formatting only"},{"h":"Layout → Margins","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"Inspect Document removes hidden data.","tag":"04"},{"q":"To require a password to OPEN a Word file, use:","opts":[{"h":"Restrict Editing","why":"controls editing, not opening"},{"h":"Protect Document → Encrypt with Password","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"Mark as Final","why":"only a warning"},{"h":"AutoSave","why":"unrelated"},{"h":"Inspect Document","why":"unrelated"}],"why":"Encrypt with Password.","tag":"04"},{"q":"Double-clicking the Format Painter button lets you:","opts":[{"h":"copy text","why":"it copies formatting"},{"h":"apply the same formatting to several places until you press Esc","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"paste unformatted text","why":"that's Paste Special"},{"h":"clear formatting","why":"different command"},{"h":"open the Styles pane","why":"different"}],"why":"Single click = once; double-click = many times.","tag":"04"},{"q":"AutoSave in Word works only when the file is saved in:","opts":[{"h":"the Desktop folder","why":"local files use AutoRecover"},{"h":"OneDrive or SharePoint","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"a USB flash drive","why":"no"},{"h":"the Recycle Bin","why":"no"},{"h":"an email attachment","why":"no"}],"why":"AutoSave = cloud files.","tag":"04"},{"q":"Which command pastes text WITHOUT its original formatting?","opts":[{"h":"Ctrl+V","why":"keeps formatting by default"},{"h":"Paste Special → Unformatted Text (or Keep Text Only)","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"Format Painter","why":"copies formatting"},{"h":"Find and Replace","why":"unrelated"},{"h":"Ctrl+G","why":"Go To"}],"why":"<code>Ctrl+Alt+V</code> opens Paste Special.","tag":"06"},{"q":"Which shortcut opens Go To in Word?","opts":[{"h":"Ctrl+F","why":"Find"},{"h":"Ctrl+H","why":"Replace"},{"h":"Ctrl+G","ok":1,"why":"Go To (F5 also works)"},{"h":"Ctrl+R","why":"align right"},{"h":"Ctrl+J","why":"justify"}],"why":"Go To: <code>Ctrl+G</code> or <code>F5</code>.","tag":"06"},{"q":"Where do you add your own AutoCorrect entries in Word?","opts":[{"h":"Home → Font","why":"no"},{"h":"File → Options → Proofing → AutoCorrect Options","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"Insert → Symbol","why":"inserts symbols"},{"h":"Review → Track Changes","why":"no"},{"h":"View → Macros","why":"no"}],"why":"AutoCorrect is in Proofing options.","tag":"06"},{"q":"Which shortcut moves to cell A1 in Excel?","opts":[{"h":"Ctrl+End","why":"last used cell"},{"h":"Ctrl+Home","ok":1,"why":"A1"},{"h":"Home","why":"start of the row only"},{"h":"Ctrl+A","why":"select all"},{"h":"F2","why":"edit cell"}],"why":"<code>Ctrl+Home</code> → A1.","tag":"07"},{"q":"What is lost when you save an Excel workbook as .csv?","opts":[{"h":"Nothing","why":"a lot is lost"},{"h":"Formatting, formulas (only values remain) and every sheet except the active one","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"Only the column widths","why":"much more is lost"},{"h":"The cell values","why":"values are kept"},{"h":"The file name","why":"no"}],"why":"CSV = plain text values, one sheet.","tag":"07"},{"q":"Which feature keeps the header row visible while you scroll?","opts":[{"h":"Split","why":"divides the window"},{"h":"Freeze Panes → Freeze Top Row","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"Wrap Text","why":"text inside a cell"},{"h":"Merge &amp; Center","why":"joins cells"},{"h":"Hide","why":"hides rows"}],"why":"View → Freeze Panes.","tag":"07"},{"q":"Which PowerPoint feature suggests ready-made layouts for the current slide?","opts":[{"h":"Slide Master","why":"edits layouts manually"},{"h":"Designer (Design Ideas)","ok":1,"why":"correct"},{"h":"Slide Sorter","why":"a view"},{"h":"Animation Pane","why":"animations"},{"h":"Outline View","why":"a view"}],"why":"Design → Designer.","tag":"11"}],"exercises":[],"challenges":[],"cheat":{"html":"<section class=\"sec sec-1-search-email-cloud\"><h2 id=\"1-search-email-cloud\">1. Search, Email &amp; Cloud</h2>\n<ul><li>Search: <code>\"exact phrase\"</code> · <code>site:edu.tr</code> · <code>filetype:pdf</code> · <code>-exclude</code>.</li><li>Email: <strong>To</strong> (action), <strong>CC</strong> (visible info), <strong>BCC</strong> (hidden list—use for bulk emails!).</li><li>Cloud sharing: <strong>Viewer</strong> (read-only) vs. <strong>Commenter</strong> vs. <strong>Editor</strong>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-2-microsoft-word\"><h2 id=\"2-microsoft-word\">2. Microsoft Word</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Table of Contents</strong>: Apply <code>Home → Styles → Heading 1/2</code>, then <code>References → Table of Contents</code>.</li><li><strong>Page Break</strong> (<code>Ctrl+Enter</code>) vs. <strong>Section Break</strong> (<code>Layout → Breaks → Next Page</code>, needed for mixed Portrait/Landscape or separate headers).</li><li><strong>Hide cover page number</strong>: Header &amp; Footer → <strong>Different First Page</strong>.</li><li><strong>Captions &amp; Citations</strong>: <code>References → Insert Caption</code> · <code>References → Insert Citation / Bibliography</code>.</li><li><strong>Review &amp; Export</strong>: <code>Review → Track Changes</code> (<code>Ctrl+Shift+E</code>) · <code>File → Export → Create PDF/XPS</code>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-3-microsoft-excel\"><h2 id=\"3-microsoft-excel\">3. Microsoft Excel</h2>\n<ul><li>Always start formulas with <strong><code>=</code></strong>. Lock fixed cells with <strong><code>$A$1</code></strong> (<code>F4</code>).</li><li>Functions: <code>SUM</code> (<code>TOPLA</code>), <code>AVERAGE</code> (<code>ORTALAMA</code>), <code>MIN</code>, <code>MAX</code>, <code>COUNT</code> (numbers), <code>COUNTA</code> (non-empty), <code>IF</code> (<code>EĞER</code>), <code>COUNTIF</code>, <code>ROUND</code>.</li><li>Sort/Filter: click 1 cell inside table → <code>Data → Filter</code> (<code>Ctrl+Shift+L</code>).</li><li>Charts: <strong>Column/Bar</strong> (compare categories), <strong>Line</strong> (time trend), <strong>Pie</strong> (% parts of whole).</li><li>Freeze header: <code>View → Freeze Panes → Freeze Top Row</code>.</li></ul>\n</section>\n<section class=\"sec sec-4-microsoft-powerpoint\"><h2 id=\"4-microsoft-powerpoint\">4. Microsoft PowerPoint</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Slide Master</strong> (<code>View → Slide Master</code>): put global logos/fonts/footers here, then <strong>Close Master View</strong>.</li><li><strong>Design</strong>: 16:9 widescreen, <strong>6×6 rule</strong>, ≥ 20 pt body font, high contrast, resize images from <strong>corner</strong> handles.</li><li><strong>Showtime</strong>: <code>F5</code> (from start), <code>Shift+F5</code> (current slide), <code>B</code> (black screen), <strong>Notes</strong> pane + <strong>Presenter View</strong>, export <code>.pdf</code> backup.</li></ul>\n</section>","title":"Office Applications — Cheat Sheet"},"mocks":{},"extra":{"formula":{"cols":6,"rows":10,"cells":{"A1":"Student","B1":"Midterm","C1":"Final","D1":"Average","E1":"Status","F1":"Rounded","A2":"Ali","B2":70,"C2":80,"A3":"Ece","B3":45,"C3":55,"A4":"Mert","B4":85,"C4":95,"A5":"Zeynep","B5":60,"C5":70,"A7":"Midterm Avg","A8":"Highest Final","A9":"Midterm >= 60","A10":"Total Final"},"tasks":[{"cell":"D2","prompt":"In D2, compute Ali's average of B2 and C2 using AVERAGE (or ORTALAMA).","model":"=AVERAGE(B2:C2)","must":"AVERAGE"},{"cell":"E2","prompt":"In E2, return \"Pass\" if D2 >= 60, otherwise \"Fail\" using IF (or EĞER).","model":"=IF(D2>=60,\"Pass\",\"Fail\")","must":"IF"},{"cell":"B7","prompt":"In B7, compute the average Midterm score across B2:B5.","model":"=AVERAGE(B2:B5)","must":"AVERAGE"},{"cell":"B8","prompt":"In B8, find the highest Final score in C2:C5 using MAX.","model":"=MAX(C2:C5)","must":"MAX"},{"cell":"B9","prompt":"In B9, count how many Midterm scores in B2:B5 are >= 60 using COUNTIF.","model":"=COUNTIF(B2:B5,\">=60\")","must":"COUNTIF"},{"cell":"B10","prompt":"In B10, calculate the sum of all Final scores in C2:C5 using SUM (or TOPLA).","model":"=SUM(C2:C5)","must":"SUM"}]},"games":{"shortcuts":{"title":"Match Office keyboard shortcuts to their actions","prompt":"Match each keyboard shortcut on the left with what it does.","pairs":[["Ctrl+H","Find and Replace (Word / Excel)"],["Ctrl+Enter","Insert a clean Page Break (Word)"],["F4 (in Excel formula)","Toggle relative/absolute $ reference ($A$1)"],["Ctrl+Shift+L","Toggle AutoFilter dropdowns (Excel)"],["F5 (PowerPoint)","Start Slide Show from the beginning"],["Shift+F5 (PowerPoint)","Start Slide Show from the current slide"],["B (during Slide Show)","Turn projector screen black to focus on speaker"]]},"ecommerce":{"title":"Match e-commerce models to real examples","prompt":"Connect each e-commerce model to its matching scenario.","pairs":[["B2C (Business-to-Consumer)","An online store selling laptops directly to students"],["B2B (Business-to-Business)","A cloud vendor selling server capacity to a university"],["C2C (Consumer-to-Consumer)","One student selling a used textbook to another online"],["C2B (Consumer-to-Business)","A freelance photographer licensing photos to a company"]]},"formats":{"title":"Match file extensions to their formats","prompt":"Match each file extension with what it stores.","pairs":[[".docx","Editable Microsoft Word document"],[".xlsx","Editable Microsoft Excel workbook"],[".pptx","Editable Microsoft PowerPoint deck"],[".pdf","Fixed-layout document that looks identical everywhere"],[".csv","Plain-text comma-separated table"],[".zip","Compressed archive bundling files and folders"]]}}}});
